    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Educational-Psychology--Tenure-Line-_R-03287": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Educational Psychology (Tenure-Line)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Educational Psychology (Tenure-Line) Compensation: $70,000-$75,000 Department: Educational Psychology Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Ball State University Department of Educational Psychology invites applications for a 9-month tenure-line faculty position in Quantitative Psychology/Quantitative Methodology. The department seeks a scholar with expertise in advanced quantitative methods who will contribute to graduate instruction, methodological research and consultation, interdisciplinary collaboration, and externally funded research. Expertise in emerging methodologies, particularly machine learning and data mining, is highly desirable. The successful candidate will teach graduate courses in statistics, quantitative methods, and research methodology in both in-person and online formats. The position will play an important role in the M.S. in Quantitative Psychology and Ph.D. in Educational Psychology programs through student advising, mentoring of master’s capstone projects, and service on doctoral committees. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active program of scholarship, pursue opportunities for external funding, and provide service to the department, college, university, and profession. The faculty member will also contribute methodological expertise to faculty research and collaborative projects within the department and across the university. This position offers substantial opportunities for interdisciplinary research and methodological collaboration. We seek a collegial scholar who will contribute to the continued development of the Quantitative Psychology program and expand the department’s methodological expertise in response to evolving research and workforce demands. Rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications and experience. Summer teaching and administrative stipends may be available consistent with university policy. The university will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching Teach three graduate-level research methodology/statistical analysis courses each fall and spring. Courses may be scheduled on campus or online. Scheduled course content could cover: Introductory Statistics Research Methodology ANOVA methodology Multiple Regression Multivariate Statistics/Data Mining Categorical Data Analysis Factor Analysis Latent Variable Modeling Psychometric/Measurement theory Longitudinal Data Analysis Multilevel Data Analysis Scholarship Maintain an active research agenda resulting in dissemination through publication in refereed journals and presentation at conferences. Grant writing and statistical consulting are also desirable. Service Lead curriculum review and continuous program improvement in MS in Quan psychology. Actively engage in university and professional service. Advisement of Masters and Doctoral Level capstone/thesis projects. Serve as a member of department, college and university committees and act as a supportive and collaborative colleague engaging in department discussion and endeavors. ​ Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Quantitative Psychology, Educational Psychology, Statistics, Research Methodology, Measurement, or a closely related field by date of appointment. At least one semester (4 months) of demonstrated experience mentoring, advising graduate students, with the ability to contribute to master’s thesis and doctoral dissertation committees. At least one semester (4 months) regarding evidence of, or potential for, effective teaching of graduate-level quantitative methods/statistics courses. Evidence of, or potential for, an active program of scholarship in quantitative methodology or its applications. Preferred Qualifications: Expertise in machine learning, data mining, and/or computational quantitative methods, particularly applications related to AI and large or complex datasets. Expertise in one or more additional areas such as psychometrics, latent variable modeling/structural equation modeling, Bayesian analysis, categorical or multivariate analysis, or meta-analysis. Experience teaching advanced quantitative methods at the graduate level, including online instruction. Evidence of successful interdisciplinary research collaboration and methodological consultation. Experience contributing quantitative/methodological expertise to externally funded research. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact Search Committee Co-chairs: Dr. Jocelyn Bolin, jebolin@bsu.edu Dr. Ophelie Desmet, ophelie.desmet@bsu.edu Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Agenda Within the application, please provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references. Note: Additional application materials may be requested later in the search process This position will remain open until filled, with a consideration date of October 28, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Schedule-Specialist-and-Academic-Affairs-Coordinator_R-03198": {
      "title": "Schedule Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Schedule Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: College of Health Deans Office_A Start Date: 10/26/2026 About this opportunity: College of Health | Ball State University The Ball State University College of Health is seeking a highly organized and detail-oriented Scheduling Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator to join the Dean's Office team. This position plays a vital role in supporting the academic and operational success of the College through course scheduling, faculty workload management, academic affairs coordination, and technology support. Key Responsibilities: -Coordinate and manage course scheduling for the College of Health. -Oversee faculty load assignments and compensation processes. -Allocate and manage classroom space to support instructional needs. -Administer affiliation agreements and contracts. -Support program accreditation, assessment, and reporting activities. -Ensure data integrity and assist with data management processes. -Coordinate technology-related needs within the College. -Train and support college staff on scheduling and faculty load procedures. The Scheduling Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator provides operational support and coordination in two primary areas: course scheduling and academic affairs administration. This role serves as a key resource for faculty, staff, and administrators by ensuring accurate scheduling, effective space utilization, compliance with accreditation requirements, and reliable data reporting. This is an excellent opportunity for a collaborative individual who enjoys working in a dynamic academic environment and contributing to student and faculty success. Join the College of Health at Ball State University and make an impact through effective coordination, organization, and support of academic operations. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The College of Health (COH) Dean's Office requires operational support and coordination in two main areas. First, as a Schedule Specialist, responsibilities include course scheduling, managing faculty load and compensation processes, and allocating classroom space. Second, in Academic Affairs Coordination, the role involves managing affiliation agreements and contracts, supporting program accreditation and assessment, ensuring data integrity and reporting, and coordinating technology. Additionally, this position includes training college staff on scheduling and faculty load procedures. Duties & Responsibilities: Schedule Specialist Related: Enter schedules and FLAC into Banner, working directly with department chairpersons and department administrative coordinators. Provide relevant data to the Associate Dean in preparation for review and oversight of schedules, course enrollment, faculty assignments, and compensation. Review, correct, and monitor the schedule of course offerings, course modality, past and current enrollments, credit hours, term dates, day and time configurations, section limits/caps, and room attributes and assignments, in consultation with department chairs, administrative coordinators, and the Associate Dean. Be aware of, and adhere to, important semester and academic deadlines, including semester course roll schedules, final course build deadlines, and priority and open registration dates. Communicate information to academic units within the college. Collaborate with the College Budget Director to maintain data in the Faculty Load and Compensation (FLAC) system Train new staff (department chairpersons, administrative coordinators, and other department staff) within COH concerning scheduling and faculty load process and policies. Provide support to Series 25 classroom space allocation and utilization software. Academic Affairs Coordinator Related: Coordinate the development, renewal, routing, execution, and maintenance of affiliation agreements, memoranda of understanding (MOUs), and other college-related contracts Coordinate annual technology and equipment requests on behalf of the college with university Information Technology and the Office of the Provost. Coordinate college assessment processes, including collecting and organizing annual assessment reports submitted by departments/schools, and providing administrative support for academic unit reviews. Support college program accreditation activities, including maintaining accurate records of program accreditation status and history, and providing administrative support to departments/schools undergoing accreditation or reaccreditation. Perform data integrity checks to ensure accuracy of academic affairs-related data in Banner. Assist the Dean and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs with data requests. Act as College Data Liaison with the Office of Institutional Research and Decision Support. General: Perform other related duties as assigned. Maintain regular and predictable attendance.    Minimum Qualifications: Associate's degree or equivalent. At least one year of office administrative, secretarial, or related experience. Excellent communication skills. Working knowledge of word processing & database management software; including common skill sets with Microsoft Office product and database management training. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Some experience using Banner and R25. Familiarity with Degree Works. Familiarity with academic procedures and college calendars. Strong communication skills. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively. How to apply: Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Jakob Lauver at jake.lauver@bsu.edu The following documents are required in this application: 1. Cover letter 2. Resume (Do not use the Autofill resume feature.) Applications must be received before 12:01AM on October 6, 2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Music--Graduate-Music-History-_R-03280": {
      "title": "Instructor of Music (Graduate Music History)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Music (Graduate Music History) Compensation: $3,000-$9,000 Department: School of Music - Temp Start Date: 01/11/2027 About this opportunity:   Ball State is seeking to hire one adjunct to teach a graduate music history course in the Spring 2027 semester . Qualifying candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: Ball State is seeking to hire one adjunct to teach a graduate music history course in the Spring 2027 semester . This course will meet one time per week on campus for 3 hours, likely during the early evening, or during the day. However, a live zoom might be possible. The instructor will propose a topic. The enrollment in the course will not exceed 15. Qualifications: A doctorate in music history/musicology Review of applications will start: 10/1/2026 How to apply:   Interested instructors should contact Dr. Heather Platt, Area Coordinator for Music History, hplatt@bsu.edu, for information about the position. Requires successful completion of a background check and education verification. Required Documents: Cover letter Resume Three references should be provided"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Emens-Laborer_R-01326": {
      "title": "Temporary Emens Laborer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Emens Laborer Compensation: $18.50 Department: Emens Auditorium - Temp Start Date: 01/12/2026 About this opportunity:   Emens Auditorium is seeking temporary laborers to work events. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: This position is for stage hands that will be responsible for loading and unloading equipment trucks and will work setting up and tearing down of production items on upcoming events performing at Emens Auditorium, Pruis Hall, and Brown Family Amphitheatre. This position may include work with hair and make-up, audio, property crew, and follow spot operators. Electrical and carpentry work may also be needed. Job Responsibilities and Duties: This position is for a wide variety of functions that is necessary for putting on a live production before an audience. Minimum Qualifications: High School graduate or equivalent (GED). Ability to lift up to 75 pounds. Position requires extended periods of standing and physical laborer. ​ Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Requires successful completion of a background check. Preferred Experience: Over 3 months of related experience. Experience in carpentry, electrical, follow spot operator, property crew, audio crew, truck loaders, pushers, backline, costumes, hair/make-up crew, and video crew. How to apply:   Required Documents: Optional Resume and Cover Letter outlining your previous work experience. Immediate positions are available."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Lecturer-Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Mathematical-Sciences_R-03272": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Mathematical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Mathematical Sciences Compensation: $50,000 - $60,000 Department: Mathematical Sciences Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Mathematical Sciences is seeking applicants for a full-time non-tenure line faculty position as Assistant Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor of Mathematical Sciences (Mathematics Education Specialization) beginning August 16, 2027. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching approximately 12 credits per term of mathematics education courses and other courses depending on Department need and applicant qualifications, including core curriculum courses such as quantitative reasoning.  Pursue a program of professional development and perform service activities for the Department.  Evidence of high-quality teaching, continuing professional development, and significant service are necessary to be eligible for reappointment. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in mathematics education or closely related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment, with at least 18 graduate semester hours of coursework in mathematics; current or previous teaching licensure or certification; at least two years of K-12 teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at the college level in undergraduate classes.  Doctorate degree in mathematics education with experience or interest teaching online.  Interest in partnerships with local schools.  Demonstrated capacity to work with diverse students as well as to prepare future educators to work with diverse populations.A   How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Jenna Menke, Search Committee Chair, jenna.menke@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below.  Important:  Do not use the autofill feature for resume. Required documents: Cover letter Teaching philosophy statement Curriculum Vitae Master’s transcript Licenses/certifications Optional documents: Doctoral transcript if applicable Additional materials supporting excellence in teaching Original transcripts showing your highest degree will be required upon hire. Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 6th, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Heat-Plant-Operator_R-03249-1": {
      "title": "Heat Plant Operator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Heat Plant Operator Compensation: $40.00 - $40.00 Department: Heat Plant Operations Start Date: 09/21/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. 3rd Shift 11:00 p.m. to 7:00 a.m. Tuesday through Saturday What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform duties required in the operation and maintenance of natural gas fired boilers, auxiliary equipment, steam and condensate return distribution system, complying with EPA , OSHA, and all appropriate operating regulations and codes. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Operate and monitor natural gas fired boilers including combustion control and pollution control equipment. Record meter readings and maintain log sheets. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, crawl, kneel, grasp, finger, lift, reach, balance, climb, talk, hear, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and Heating Plant instrumentation and testing equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 2. O perating heat plant auxiliary equipment (water treatment, feed water pumps, air compressors, valves, emergency power generating equipment, etc.) Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, balance, climb, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, and scaffolds. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 3.  Performing duties related to the construction, replacement, repair, and maintenance of all types of steam distribution equipment; perform maintenance duties such as pump, turbine, compressor and fan rebuilding. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, balance, climb, talk, hear, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and Heating Plant instrumentation and testing equipment. Employee is exposed inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 4. Performing duties related to the replacement and repair of the boiler furnace refractory; install sludge drying equipment. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, climb, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand tools and Heating Plant instrumentation. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 5. Performing pipe fitting, welding, metal work, rigging, low voltage electrical work, insulating and painting tasks. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, balance, climb, talk, hear, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and Heating Plant instrumentation. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 6. Performing water treatment tests, adding chemicals, maintaining water treatment equipment. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, finger, grasp, work with arms and hands extended, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand tools, painting, cleaning, lubricating, and vibration equipment, ladders, scaffolds, and Heating Plant instrumentation and testing equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 7. Maintaining cleanliness and orderliness of work areas, equipment, and vehicles. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, crawl, kneel, grasp, finger, lift, reach, climb, balance, talk, hear, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, distinguish color, and align parts and equipment. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, welding machines, cutting torches, and Heating Plant instrumentation and testing equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 8. Acquire and maintain knowledge of various job-related chemicals, environmental concerns, and current technological improvements/advancements. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print, distinguish color, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 9. Demonstrate through periodic examination proficiency in all aspects of the operation including but not limited to boiler operation, plant operation and emergency procedures. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print, distinguish color, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 10 . Perform other duties as assigned. May require any or all of the above-mentioned abilities. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent (GED ). 1.Successful completion of an apprenticeship program as Stationary Engineer as approved by the Bureau of Apprenticeship and Training, or at least six (6) years of verified proof of experience in operation and maintenance of a gas, and/or oil fired boiler plant or related equipment, or equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 2.Must possess and maintain a valid Indiana Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 3.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures, and communications, and perform mathematical calculations. 4.Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty/responsibility. 5.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: Vocational school training 1.More than six (6) years of verified proof of experience in operation and maintenance of a gas, and/or oil-fired boiler plant or related equipment. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Devon Johnson, Assistant Manager of Plant Operations at 765-285-6176 or devon.johnson@bsu.edu . Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
