    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Music--Director-of-Bands-_R-03412": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Music (Director of Bands)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Music (Director of Bands) Compensation: $65,000 - $67,000 Department: School of Music Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The School of Music invites applications for a full-time Tenure Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Music (Director of Bands) beginning August of 2027. The School of Music is committed to maintaining a positive, collaborative, and inclusive work environment where your success is supported. This is a full-time opportunity that comes with a great benefits package. Come be a part of our team! This position requires on-campus presence. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: The Assistant/Associate Professor of Music and Director of Bands will direct the Ball State Wind Ensemble and provide oversight and leadership of the comprehensive university band program, instruct undergraduate and graduate courses in instrumental conducting, participate in recruitment activities and teach other courses as assigned.   Duties and Responsibilities: ·         Direction of the Ball State Wind Ensemble ·         Oversight and leadership of the comprehensive university band program, including five ensembles ·         Lead the graduate winds conducting program, including doctoral and master’s-level students ·         Participate in recruitment activities for instrumental students at the undergraduate and graduate levels ·         Instruct undergraduate and graduate courses in instrumental conducting ·         Teach other courses as assigned, based on the needs of the school and the expertise of the candidate ·         Engage in creative and/or scholarly activities ·         Contribute to service at the university, regional, and national levels ·         Supervise graduate assistants, who have significant teaching roles in our curriculum.   Minimum Qualifications: ·         Master's degree in Music ·         A minimum of 4 years of successful experience in collegiate wind ensemble conducting   Preferred Qualifications: ·         Terminal degree in music (DMA, DA, or Ph.D.) ·         5 years of successful collegiate wind ensemble conducting experience ·         Experience of successful teaching of conducting courses at undergraduate and graduate level ·         Record of collegiate ensembles performing at Regional and/or National Conferences ·         Evidence of creative/scholarly productivity in the wind ensemble field ·         Experience with student recruitment and program development How to apply: Please direct inquiries regarding this vacancy to Dr. Franklin Larey, Director of the School of Music, franklin.larey@bsu.edu The following application materials are required: Cover letter of application Curriculum vitae (Do not use the Autofill resume feature.) Portfolio: a supplemental document containing links to frontal-view video recordings including: Two (only) conducting performances with repertoire of contrasting style Two (only) continuous unedited rehearsal segments of 10-15 minutes each If possible, one additional segment showing the candidate providing instruction in conducting In addition, applicants are asked to provide the contact information of at least three referees.   Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by December 1, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits