    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Associate-Professor-and-Program-Director-of-Counseling-Psychology_R-03284": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor and Program Director of Counseling Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant/Associate Professor and Program Director of Counseling Psychology Compensation: $65,000 - $82,000 Department: Counsel Psych, Social Psych & Couns Start Date: 08/23/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Counseling Psychology, Social Psychology, and Counseling invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor who will serve as the next Program Director of Counseling Psychology for our APA accredited PhD program. Employer will consider sponsorship. The Department of Counseling Psychology, Social Psychology and Counseling: We train students to become competent scientist-professional counseling psychologists who assist people in the context of their relationships, communities, and the larger world. The department’s mission is to make a significant contribution to the fields of psychology and counseling through research, practice, service, and teaching grounded in developmental, systems, holistic, and strength-based theories and strategies. The Department is housed in the College of Health. The College of Health: A vital health resource for Indiana in preparing health professionals, the College of Health is moving boldly forward in making interprofessional education, practice and research its paradigm across its disciplines. The college offers 32 academic programs in seven units: the Departments of Counseling Psychology, Social Psychology, and Counseling; Military Science; Nutrition and Health Science; Speech Pathology and Audiology; and Social Work, plus the Schools of Nursing and Kinesiology. Our 224 faculty and staff serve nearly 3,000 students. We partner with regional communities for immersive learning and research. Our Health Professions Building opened in 2019 with 165,000 square feet and is LEED Gold certified. Our Interprofessional Community Clinics offer a range of health and mental health services provided by students under faculty supervision, as well as community health education and prevention services through the Healthy Lifestyle Center. Other facilities include the Health and Physical Activity complex, Ball Gymnasium, and Lewellen Aquatic Center. Our faculty and students contribute to the evidence base for their respective disciplines, and our research footprint includes the Center for Peace and Conflict Studies and the Human Performance Laboratory. We intend to contribute to a well-prepared health professional workforce that helps decrease health care disparities. Ball State University: Ball State University is located in Muncie, Indiana, on an attractive campus 45 miles northeast of Indianapolis. Ball State enjoys a close relationship with the City of Muncie, and many employees extol the virtues of living in this Midwestern college town of about 70,000 people. Institutionally, Ball State has established ambitious goals for its second century through its strategic plan, Destination 2040: Our Flight Path. We pledge to provide a premier educational experience for every student, to partner with the community to improve the lives of our neighbors, and to maintain a lifelong presence in the lives of our alumni. Ball State engages students in educational, research, and creative endeavors that empower our graduates to have fulfilling careers and meaningful lives enriched by lifelong learning and service, while we enhance the economic, environmental, and social vitality of our community, our state, and our world. Information about working at Ball State and relocating to East Central Indiana is available at: https://www.bsu.edu/about/jobsatballstate What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: A. Teaching: Courses in the counseling psychology and counseling core, and courses consistent with teaching expertise in relevant area; participation in departmental clinic training activities. B. Research: Conduct, publish, and present scholarly research. Keep abreast of recent scholarly developments in areas of specialty and incorporate into teaching. C. Service: Actively contribute to the intellectual and professional life of the Department, College of Health, Ball State University, and the surrounding community through general service and preventative, developmental, and outreach activities. Participate in local and national professional service activities. Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in counseling psychology from an APA accredited program in Counseling Psychology by August 15, 2027. ABD candidates will be considered only if all degree requirements will be completed by August 15, 2027. Professional competence to teach advanced doctoral practicum and other courses in the program as needed and provide clinical supervision to doctoral students in the department’s training clinic. Competence in a specialty area within counseling psychology as demonstrated by publications and professional conference presentations. License-eligible as a Health Service Provider in Psychology in the State of Indiana. Preferred Qualifications: Ability to contribute to the department’s counseling psychology scientist-professional training model. Demonstrated research, teaching, and mentoring experiences with graduate students. Prior leadership and administrative experience. While the area of specialization is open, special consideration will be given to candidates who can contribute to all graduate programs in the department with the ability to mentor students, facilitate immersive learning experiences, and teach courses and train students in (a) advanced counseling interventions, (b) psychological assessment, (c) health psychology, (d) couples and families, (e) multicultural issues, and/or (f) children/adolescents.   How to apply: For inquiries regarding this vacancy, please contact the search committee chair, Larry Gerstein, Ph.D. (lgerstein@bsu.edu). Required Documents: 1. Cover letter- describe your interest in the department and serving as the training director, your leadership philosophy and qualifications for the position, and your relevant scholarly, teaching and clinical experience. 2. Vitae with publications and/or professional conference presentations cited. (Do not use the Autofill resume feature) Optional Documents: 1.Copy of official graduate transcripts (Official transcripts are required upon hire.) Within this application, names and contact information for three professional references will be requested. References will not be contacted without prior notice to the applicant. Finalists will be asked to submit additional materials, which may include a description of their scholarship, evidence of teaching effectiveness, letters of reference, or verification of licensure status. Consideration Date : to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by: November 30, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Associate-Clinical-Professor-of-Athletic-Training-and-Graduate-Athletic-Training-Program-Director_R-03500": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor of Athletic Training and Graduate Athletic Training Program Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor of Athletic Training and Graduate Athletic Training Program Director Compensation: $60,000 - $75,000 Department: School of Kinesiology Start Date: 08/15/2027 About this opportunity: The School of Kinesiology welcomes applications for a full-time non-tenure-line Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor of Athletic Training and Graduate Athletic Training Program Director, which is part of the College of Health at Ball State University. Our CAATE-accredited Master of Science in Athletic Training (MSAT) is a two-year professional program preparing students for successful careers as athletic trainers. Following a successful comprehensive CAATE self-study and accreditation review, the program continues to build on its strengths and history through innovative curriculum, high-quality clinical education, and continuous program improvement. Our students gain diverse, hands-on experiences while learning from dedicated faculty and preceptors committed to developing confident, collaborative, advanced-practice healthcare professionals. The ideal candidate will possess a combination of academic administration and teaching experience. Courses will be taught face-to-face and blended online. The position will begin in August 2027, with possible summer administration and teaching in 2027, and includes salary commensurate with experience, a full benefits package, and opportunities for additional summer compensation. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: The Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor of Athletic Training and Graduate Athletic Training Program Director will be expected to teach in the Graduate Athletic Training program and provide strategic leadership and administration for the program, ensuring full compliance with CAATE standards and institutional policies. They will 1) direct program planning, curriculum development, and continuous quality improvement while guiding faculty in assessment, curriculum mapping, and accreditation activities; 2) oversee the full student lifecycle, from recruitment, marketing, and admissions to retention, academic advising, and Board of Certification (BOC) outcomes, while collaborating with the Director of Clinical Education to integrate didactic and clinical training; and 3) manage program resources, including budgets, facilities, equipment, and technology, while serving as the primary liaison and representative to institutional stakeholders and external professional organizations.   The rank for this non-tenure line faculty position is Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor of Athletic Training. This position reports to the Chair of the School of Kinesiology. Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctoral degree or completion of doctoral degree requirements in athletic training and/or related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment; Experience in administration and teaching in a Commission on Accreditation of Athletic Training Education (CAATE) accredited athletic training program (professional, post-professional or residency); Five years of experience as a BOC-Certified Athletic Trainer; Current Board of Certification (BOC) recognition as a Certified Athletic Trainer; Eligible to be licensed in the state of Indiana as an athletic trainer.   Preferred Qualifications: Five plus years of experience in Athletic Training Program Administration/Accreditation, such as Program Director, Coordinator of Clinical Education or core faculty; Experience and familiarity with CAATE standards and accreditation requirements; Teaching or clinical expertise in musculoskeletal evaluation; NPI number How to apply: Questions about the position may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Stacy Walker, at sewalker@bsu.edu .  The following application materials are required: Cover letter of application describing your interest in the position and how you meet the qualifications for this position, Curriculum vitae (Do not use the Autofill resume feature.) In addition, applicants are asked to provide the contact information of at least three individuals willing to serve as professional references. Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 16, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. ) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Honors-College-Advisor_R-03502": {
      "title": "Honors College Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Honors College Advisor Compensation: $44,000-$46,000 Department: Honors College About this opportunity: The Honors College at Ball State University welcomes applications for Honors College Advisor. We seek an engaged professional who is committed to supporting students on their way to completing an Honors Diploma. This position will join a dynamic team of advisors who work together to support students in the Honors College. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Serve as one of three professional academic advisors to all Honors College students (matriculates, transfer, and upper division students) in academic program planning, course scheduling, and other academic activities; participate in summer orientation and summer advising; support the Dean of the Honors College in providing services to Honors students; collaborate with University College’s Office of Academic Advising in understanding and interpreting curriculum requirements. Duties/Responsibilities: Meet individually with Honors College students for degree planning, curricular monitoring, and academic counseling. Maintain knowledge about degree requirements in all Ball State majors and university systems as they pertain to course scheduling, course selection, and other functions of university software that are appropriate to professional advisors. Direct and participate in the advising portion of new student orientation; train and supervise summer advisors. Review updated matriculate data to determine necessary schedule adjustments. Tutor new Honors students on interpreting the degree audit program; consult on creation and development of four-year plans for graduation. Review and enter four-year plans for first year Honors students into the student degree management software system. Promote strategies for retention (for example, individual interview sessions to address the following: time management, test anxiety, study skills development, decision-making skills development, career exploration). Contact students who have received a midterm deficiency to identify the causes of the deficiency and develop corrective strategies. Contact students who have not registered for classes and facilitate the registration process. Attend Honors College staff meetings and inform Honors College staff of current and pending issues arising from advising. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree requirements from an accredited college or university completed at time of appointment. One year relevant experience (for example, teaching, counseling or advising). ​ Excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree requirements from a regionally accredited college or university completed at time of appointment. Direct experience advising college-level students. Demonstrable commitment to Honors education. Knowledge of Ball State’s Honors College, Honors academic requirements, and university requirements Experience working with student information and degree management software systems Familiarity with Ball State’s current student information and degree management software systems. How to apply: For questions regarding this opportunity please contact Richard Petts, Interim Dean, at rjpetts@bsu. edu. The following documents are required: 1. Cover letter 2. Resume (Do not use the Autofill Resume feature.) Applications must be received before 12:01 AM on November 9, 2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Sports-Facilities-Supervisor_R-03504": {
      "title": "Sports Facilities Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Sports Facilities Supervisor Salary Grade: Exempt Staff 10 Compensation: $35,568.00 - 38,038.00 Department: Recreation Services_A Start Date: 11/08/2026 About this opportunity: Working for Ball State offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical and prescription coverage, dental and vision insurance, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, a university-funded retirement plan, large tuition discounts, and more! Recreation Services has an opening for a Sports Facilities Supervisor to oversee a talented team of Field Facilities Attendants and student employees to ensure cleanliness, attractiveness, and timely set-ups of all athletic, recreation or physical education venues and special events, facilities, courts, or fields. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Assign, monitor, direct, train, and evaluate work of Field Facilities Attendants and student employees to ensure cleanliness, attractiveness, and timely set-ups of all athletic, recreation or physical education venues and special events, facilities, courts, or fields. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Plan, organize, assign, and review daily project work assignments of Field/Facilities Attendants and students. 2. Supervise, monitor, inspect, and coordinate daily operations, including special event set-ups and takedowns, ensuring methods, supplies, and equipment are properly utilized. 3. Assist with the proper allocation of Field Facilities Attendants for specific work assignments necessitated by emergency or special events. 4. Coordinate and inspect proper marking and set-ups of all athletic, recreation or physical education venues, courts, or fields according to established athletic and academic guidelines or standards. 5. Assist with the supervision and coordination of proper operations of Physical Education, Athletic and Recreation facilities and spaces. 6. Maintain records of employees, equipment, and supplies; includes attendance, overtime equalization charts, vacation schedules, performance records, disciplinary action reports, formal documentation, equipment and supplies evaluations, new product recommendations, and building maintenance/repair orders. 7. Orient and train staff, and make recommendations in all areas related to supervision, including but not limited to assisting with compensation, discipline, performance appraisals, training, and career development of Field Facilities Attendants and students. 8. Monitor and report personnel concerns, equipment and supply needs, and the need for maintenance and repair of physical facilities. 9. Monitor and enforce all safety, shop, and university rules and regulations and report problems to the Associate Director of Sports Facilities and Recreation and resolve problems appropriately. 10. Assist with the interviewing and hiring of employees and students as necessary. 11. Act as a liaison with various departments on campus with regard to general maintenance and operational issues. 12. Perform other related duties as assigned. 13. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Eighteen months of training or education beyond high school or equivalent. Three through five years of experience in building services and grounds maintenance, including at least one year of first-line supervisory experience. Must possess and maintain a valid Indiana Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree More than one year first-line supervisory experience; experience working with bargaining unit employees; experience working in a high school, university, or sports/recreation environment; personal computer and software proficiency.   How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Director of Sports, Recreation, and Concessions Building Services and Programs, Brandon L. Johnson bljohnson@bsu.edu 765-285-4221 Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below.  Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume.   Required Document: 1. Resume Optional Document (Recommended for Best Consideration): 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/University-Dining-Supervisor_R-03446": {
      "title": "University Dining Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: University Dining Supervisor Compensation: $43,888 Department: Ball State University Dining_H About this opportunity: Ball State University has a professional leadership opportunity available in Ball State University Dining that offers an excellent benefits package, paid time off and the opportunity for work/life balance. The University Dining Supervisor position is responsible for directing, overseeing, and leading all food and beverage operations within Ball State University Dining. This position is an evening/closing supervisor. The successful candidate will lead and direct subordinates resulting in good organization and minimal stress, promote teamwork, and execute excellent customer service that exceeds customer expectations. To learn more about Ball State University Dining, please visit our website at: http://www.bsu.edu/campuslife/dining . This position supervises full-time and part-time food service workers, cashiers, custodians, group leaders and student employees. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under the direction of the General Manager, oversee and supervise employees in achieving excellence in customer satisfaction, food quality, service of food, employee efficiency and productivity, financial goals, and compliance with safety and sanitation standards, HACCP standards, Indiana Food Service Code regulations, and rules, policies and procedures of Ball State University: additional functions include but are not limited to food service forecasting and record keeping, physical inventory, subordinate training, food and supply purchasing, communication, executing promotions and advertisements, complying with branded concept license and franchise agreements and standards of operations, executing detailed plans and arrangements, contributing to menu, recipe, and concept development, and participating on a limited basis in preparation and serving of food or cashiering. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Lead and supervise employees in executing correct, timely procedures in meeting license/franchise and department standards in relation to the preparation and service of all menu items, including but not limited to recipe preparation, food presentation, quality control, customer service, and sanitation and safety as defined by BSU manuals, handbooks, HACCP standards, Indiana Food Code, NRA ServSafe, and other industry standards; employ excellence in management techniques to exhibit evidence of teamwork and execution of excellent customer service that exceeds customer expectations in such areas, including but not limited to courtesy, speed of service, sense of urgency, product consistency, demonstrating a passion for excellence, utilizing fun and humor when appropriate, innovation and creativity, and other criteria. 2. Orient, coach, and train employees resulting in well-trained employees who consistently exhibit excellence in job knowledge and performance; ensure employees are well trained before working in any job assignment; provide accurate, balanced (positive and negative) feedback to employees regarding job performance and follow up on corrective measures; complete and maintain file documentation for all orientation, coaching, and training of each employee according to departmental procedures. 3. Count safe and audit safe record; audit cashier reports and submit thorough, accurate, cashier check-out reports to bookkeeper; properly report and account for shortages in safe or deposits of sales; complete documentation, report all unaccounted monies (over $20.00) immediately to the General Manager and/or University Police; check and approve all cashier refunds to customers and audit the no sale transactions of each cashier to prevent cashier theft; maintain accurate and up-to-date meal card system, including but not limited to reporting lost cards, verify account status, and overseeing the recording of off line transactions; administer university and departmental policies as they relate to money handling and reporting; ensure cashiers properly ring sales to record product movement and product value related to each brand upon which royalty payments to brand licensors or franchisors are based. 4. Utilize the Cbord Menu Management computer system to prepare menu item forecasts to (a) determine production of foods for service, and (b) correctly submit service statistics for historical data via computer record; under firm deadlines, scrutinize purchase requisitions and approve amounts of foods and supplies to be ordered based upon forecasted projections of sales and menu items, inventory levels, and other indicators; manage purchasing assignment with the utmost in business ethics and following policies and procedures of Ball State University; maintain appropriate inventory levels of foods and supplies as assigned, with neither being over or under-stocked; complete weekly inventory of foods and/or supplies with a high degree of accuracy. 5. Oversee and maintain adequate staffing following University procedures to schedule replacement employees; complete documentation related to scheduling regular and overtime staff; maintain correct telephone and address lists of all employees to facilitate this task; demonstrate a commitment to affirmative action and equal employment opportunity; communicate with peers and subordinates in a thorough, detailed, timely even-handed manner resulting in effective personal contact and/or the completion of management log entries that communicate necessary information to peers; attend shift meetings, unit and departmental management staff meetings, and relate telephone messages and/or other information accurately and in a timely manner; maintain confidentiality and ethical practices as relates to communications; in stressful situations, remain, calm, in control, and have a positive impact on others; manage disagreements effectively and create an environment where peers, employees, and customers are treated with dignity and respect and where rules, policies, and procedures are consistently administered. 6. Evaluate, investigate, and secure approval of General Manager and the Assistant Director of Personnel, or the Director, then issue warranted counseling or discipline to employees in a timely manner according to university policies and procedures; submit written documentation of all investigations, interviews, meetings, or conversations related to the situation in addition to copies of the properly issued disciplinary forms; accurately administer the union agreement and addenda thereto (including absence and tardiness policies and required record-keeping). 7. Unlock facility for the day’s operations and/or secure the facility for the periods of closure; observe safety and security precautions to prevent personal or employee injury, and theft of university or employee property; maintain personal and unit keys in a safe manner to prevent unauthorized use. 8. Establish, evaluate, and execute personal and unit goals, and contribute to departmental goal setting and achievement; serve in a contributory and effective manner on teams, committees, and task forces; demonstrate a professional appearance; wear clean, well-pressed clothing daily; follow prescribed dress code guidelines as outlined in departmental policies, rules, and regulations. 9. Evaluate employee performance and complete timely formal appraisal forms impartially and in an unbiased manner; submit draft appraisals for the approval of the General Manager; properly conduct the performance review meetings with employees; route completed forms in a timely manner. 10. Contribute to optimizing profitability through effective monitoring and supervision of food waste, portion control, inventory management, key control, theft and security controls, proper charging of sales to customers and employees by cashiers, and employees as they use and care for the facility, equipment, and furnishings; assist in evaluating food, labor, and other controllable costs; implement corrective measures as needed. 11. Collaborate in executing an effective marketing and promotion program for the unit in conjunction with the General Manager, approval from the Assistant Director of Personnel, and Assistant Director of Operations. 12. Provide planning of standard and custom menus, submit recipes for new menu items, and assist with development of sales mix for the unit; assist in planning and executing special events, catered events, and other non-routine food services. 13. Coordinate an effective laundry procedure to ensure proper supply of clean linen; maintain neat, accurate, require records; report maintenance and repair needs of building and equipment in a timely manner. 14. Perform food preparation, service and cashiering duties in emergency situations, and/or for short work periods to meet customer demand. 15. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: -Associates degree from an accredited institution or equivalent combination of education, credentials, certification, and experience. -At least one year of direct or related work experience (exclusive of teaching) in commercial or institutional food service, with demonstrated leadership and dynamic team building skills. -Skills in oral and written communication, strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: -Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. -Five years of direct or related work experience (exclusive of teaching) in commercial or institutional food service, with demonstrated leadership and dynamic team building skills supervisory experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Dining at 765-285-1967. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Science-Education_R-03388": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Science Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Science Education Compensation: $65,000 - $72,000 Department: Biology Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Ball State University Department of Biology, in collaboration with the STEM Education Center, is seeking applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Science Education beginning August 2027. This is a full-time, on-campus, nine-month, benefit-eligible position offering a competitive salary. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses within science education, including secondary and elementary methods courses as well as a biology content course for elementary educators. There may be opportunities for teaching other undergraduate and graduate courses, supervising student teachers, or supporting programs in local school districts through our professional development school relationships. The successful candidate will also develop an externally funded, science education research program, ideally engaging undergraduate and graduate students while complementing and collaborating with current faculty in the Department of Biology and the STEM Education Center. The strongest candidates will bring accomplished K-12 experience, engagement with local schools, and a record of peer-reviewed publications supporting a well-defined science education research program with strong potential for external funding. Duties and Responsibilities: Will teach undergraduate courses in science education for secondary and/or elementary teachers. The teaching assignment may include: Introduction to Science Teaching, Methods of Secondary Science Teaching, Curriculum & Research, and Using Science Methods and Materials. Methods courses are paired with field experiences, and address planning, instruction, and assessment in the science classroom, among other topics. Typical load is 3 courses (9 credit hours) per semester. Department, Facilities, and Support The Department of Biology comprises 30 full-time faculty, including multiple faculty focused on science education, and offers the BS in Biology, the MS in Biology, and the PhD in Environmental Sciences. The Ball State STEM Education Center is the home of the interdisciplinary Teaching Major in Science, with concentrations in middle school science, chemistry, Earth/space science, life science, and physics. The successful candidate will have access to: Foundational Sciences Building . The Department of Biology is housed within the Foundational Sciences Building, which includes more than 70 teaching and research labs, specific labs for science education methods courses, additional space for collaboration and conferencing, and Foundational Sciences Research Library. This building, completed in 2021, is a beautiful campus space for research, collaboration, and teaching. STEM Education Center . The Ball State STEM Education Center serves as a STEM education hub and involves an interdisciplinary network of faculty. The Center supports STEM teacher preparation, community engagement, K-12 school partnerships, and STEM education scholarship. The Center’s mission is to expand access to high-quality STEM teaching, prepare the next generation of outstanding STEM teachers, and position Ball State as a state and national leader in STEM education. Local School District Partnership . Ball State University has a formal partnership with the Muncie Community Schools district that provides collaborative opportunities for scholarship, outreach and engagement. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in Science Education or a closely related field by the date of appointment. At least 24 months of experience teaching in a K-12 setting. Preferred Qualifications Current or previous teaching K-12 licensure or certification. Undergraduate teaching experience relevant to science teacher preparation. Partnership experience with K-12 public schools. Record of science education scholarship related to K-12 teacher preparation / professional development (e.g., peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, postdoctoral research, or comparable scholarly accomplishment). Experience applying for external research grants (funded proposals are an additional strength). How to apply: Questions about the position may be directed to Tim Carter, tccarter@bsu.edu, Chair of the Department of Biology. Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Applications should include: Cover letter addressing the stated responsibilities and qualifications. Curriculum vitae A research statement (2 single-spaced page max). A teaching statement (2 single-spaced page max). Applications must be received by November 30, 2026, at 12:01 AM. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Event-Staff_R-03357": {
      "title": "Temporary Event Staff",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Event Staff Compensation: $15.00 Department: Sports Facilities Management - Temp Start Date: 10/09/2026 About this opportunity:   Ball State University is seeking individuals to work as temporary workers for special events and athletic events. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: Maintain a safe environment for special events at the University. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Provide security and direction at special events for Sports Facilities Management. Check patrons as they enter facilities. Seat patrons according to ticket location. Maintain Safety during special events. Secure facilities. Assist with event set-up and take-down when needed. Scanning and clicking tickets. Checking bags as patrons enter the facilities. Working miscellaneous events needing security, bag check, etc. Perform other related duties assigned Minimum Qualifications: Must be able to stand for long periods. Must be able to work 3 of the 5 home football games. How to apply:   Cover letter and resume are optional. Requires successful completion of a background check. NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Substitute-Bus-Driver_R-03482": {
      "title": "Temporary Substitute Bus Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Substitute Bus Driver Compensation: Department: General Institutional Support - Temp Start Date: 10/26/2026 About this opportunity:   Ball State University welcomes applications for Temporary Substitute Bus Drivers. At Ball State University our Temporary Substitute Bus Drivers will operate Ball State University buses to transport students, faculty, staff, and personnel on the shuttle run or other dispatched runs. Work hours and days are as assigned per bus requests. There is no set schedule or shift. Number of hours per week varies; could be 0 hours to 40+ hours a week depending on demands. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function: Operate Ball State University buses to transport students, faculty, staff, and personnel on the shuttle run or other dispatched runs. Rate of pay for position is: $20.74. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Operate passenger buses, shuttles, vans and paratransit units on various routes as established by the Transportation Office. 2. Inspect buses and report any equipment malfunctions; maintain cleanliness of vehicles. 3. Fuel daily and inspect bus for any exterior damage. 4. Maintain contact with Transportation Office when necessary via radio and/or telephone; inform office of changes in location, delays, traffic problems, emergencies, etc. 5. Maintain accurate records of mileage and number of passengers; complete various trip sheets and logs for each assigned task. 6. Assist and direct disabled individuals on and off vehicles as needed. 7. Report any problems with routes and make recommendations for changes when appropriate. 8. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School Diploma or Equivalent (GED) 2. At least six months of verified professional driving experience. 3. Must demonstrate ability to drive bus (on-site driving test). 4. Must possess and maintain a valid CDL (Commercial Driver’s License) with an endorsement for public passengers and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 5. Must possess a good driving record; verification through Bureau of Motor Vehicles. 6. Must pass a post offer/pre-employment mandatory drug and alcohol test. 7. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. Preferred Qualifications: Over-the-road (OTR) bus or truck driving experience. How to apply:   For inquiries, please contact: Mike Hill, Supervisor of Bus Operations at 765-285-6005, mdhill5@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover Letter (optional) Resume"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Office-Coordinator_R-03518": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Office Coordinator Salary Grade: Staff 10 Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: Fraternity & Sorority Life Start Date: 11/17/2026 About this opportunity: The Office Coordinator with the Office of Student Life position will help to overseeing daily office functions, including, but not limited to: budget processing, customer service, and direct assistance with campus and community partners. This role will interact with staff, students, families, and community partners on a regular basis. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide secretarial functions for the Office of Student Life including support of 4 professional staff members by coordinating office organizational activities such as scheduling appointments, performing clerical duties, and follow-up with students and other areas needing assistance; assist and maintain financial records for organizations; and assist in the management of office budget foundational funds, and external grant funds. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Perform secretarial duties for the professional staff; includes compose, edit, proof, and finalize correspondence, answer telephone, maintain calendar, file, and receive visitors. 2. Manage three departmental financial accounts, six student organizations accounts, and various Ball State Foundation accounts; administer invoice payments and reimbursement processing utilizing the SciQuest system; monitor and reconcile expenditures and revenue in Banner system; track expenditures for four purchasing cards; analyze charges for compliance of BSU Procurement card procedures. Verify and reconcile monthly charges, process fund transfers via JP Morgan Chase Smart Data system, inquire and remedy incorrect charges and/or disputes; upload monthly receipts into Document Management System. 3. Provide quality and professional customer service to all guests. 4. Coordinate transportation for assigned professional staff and assist with travel for registered student organizations; utilize Banner Travel system to complete travel authorizations, travel expense reports including reimbursement processing, and vehicle reservations through Fleet Commander and driver’s license approval. 5. Maintain, monitor and facilitate any and all purchases, repairs, and functions for office equipment; responsible for upkeep, ordering and keeping track of office supplies and materials for fraternity and sorority life, excellence in leadership, and service opportunities. 6. Coordinate with professional staff for the use of the volunteer management system in regard to service opportunities for students, logging volunteer hours, and working directly with agencies. Work with outside community agencies to host and upload service opportunities on the volunteer management system. 7 . In conjunction with the Office Coordinator of Student Life, interview, hire, and train students. Direct work of student employees. 8. Organize, manage, and maintain accurate record keeping system for key distributions of all  OSL  employees and necessary student organizations. 9. Coordinate information for all allocated office space for student organizations. 10. Perform other related duties as assigned. 11. Maintain regular and predictable attendance.   Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or equivalent. Over one through three years of office organizational, secretarial or related experience. Proficient in Microsoft Word and Excel: excellent communication and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree or equivalent in office administration, or related field. Additional years of related secretarial experience; knowledge of Banner System. How to apply: Questions regarding this position may be directed to: Search Committee Chair Kara L. Westfall Senior Associate Director of Student Life klwestfall@bsu.edu 765-285-2621 Initial interviews may take place during the posting period. If selected for a first round interview, you will be contacted by email to schedule a phone interview. Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Please follow the upload instructions to attach the required supporting document listed below. Required Document: Resume Optional Document (preferred): Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Philosophy_R-03540": {
      "title": "Instructor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Philosophy Compensation: $3,000 per class Department: English - Temp Start Date: 01/11/2027 About this opportunity:   Ball State University is seeking a part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Instructor of Philosophy to teach one class in Spring 2027 semester. This position will be for one semester. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Compensation for the Spring 2027 semester will be $3,000 per class. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Duties and Responsibilities: Teach one class Spring 2027 semester Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Philosophy from an accredited college or university by date of appointment. One year experience teaching at the college level. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Philosophy from an accredited college or university by date of appointment. Three or more years’ experience in teaching ethics or introduction to philosophy at the college level. How to apply:   For inquiries about the position please contact Kevin Smith at ksmith@bsu.edu Required Documents : NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume.   Cover Letter Resume Applications must be received by 12:01 am on November 28, 2026"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Food-Service-Cashier_R-03474-1": {
      "title": "Food Service Cashier",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Food Service Cashier Compensation: $17.29 - $17.29 Department: Ball State University Dining_H Start Date: 10/23/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Dining has an opportunity for a Cashier position. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefit package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! The ideal candidate will possess great customer service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on-campus opportunity. Hours: (Two week) Sunday: Off Monday: 10:30a-7p Tuesday: 10:30a-7p Wednesday: 10:30a-7p Thursday: 10:30a-7p Friday: 8a-4:30p Saturday: Off Sunday: Off Monday: 10:30a-7p Tuesday: 10:30a-7p Wednesday: 10:30a-7p Thursday: 10:30a-7p Friday: 8a-4:30p Saturday: Off Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform duties related to collection and recording of monies. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Count, wrap, and verify money. Keep money and reports secure at all times. Requires the ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, efficiently operate a calculator, read and comprehend written materials, and be detail-oriented. 2. Open on time and maintain published meal service hours. Requires the ability to walk/stand for extended periods of time. Task requires the visual ability to direct customers to key areas. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. 3. Operate electronic terminals with a high degree of accuracy in logging on, completing cash transactions, completing cash equivalency and debit account transactions, and generating a detailed daily media report at the end of each meal. A high degree of accuracy is expected. Requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, have dexterity and strength in hands, and exert up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and 10 pounds of force frequently. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth. 4. Prepare a manual ‘Check Out Form’ to report all monies from sales and to account for sales ‘overage’ and ‘shortage’. Form must be neatly written and completely accurate. Frequent overage or shortage is not acceptable. Requires the ability to read and comprehend written materials, perform basic mathematical calculations, grasp and handle objects, and be detail-oriented. Task requires the ability to provide written instructions and information. 5. Customer transactions must be made speedily; interact with customers with a smile, courtesy, friendliness, and helpfulness, and communicate customer concerns, questions, comments, and compliments to supervisor. Requires the ability to use computerized card reader, cash register, terminals, calculators, and scales. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions. 6. Maintain cash terminal, scales (where applicable), and other equipment in good condition through correct operation and cleaning procedures. Report equipment malfunctions immediately. Requires the ability to read and comprehend written materials and efficiently operate computerized machinery. Task requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, and have dexterity and strength in hands. 7. Maintain cleanliness, neatness, attractive product display, and good organization of all areas around and including cashier station. May require any of the above-mentioned abilities . 8. Enforce all rules and regulations, including but not limited to: observation of the servery, dining room and grocery areas for possible theft such as pocketing food items or not paying; In all-you-care-to-eat locations, admit only those who have a valid meal plan or who have paid; Permit carry-out according to policy and procedures; Report all violations immediately to management. May require any of the above-mentioned abilities. 9. May be required to: wash and clean dining room conveyors, tables, chairs, service areas, other furnishings, window sills, plants, and equipment located in dining room, serve or re-supply food, snack foods, and other items, instruct dining room attendants in performance of work, assist with special meals or events, i.e., napkin folding, draping and skirting tables, placing decorations, dishing foods, setting up buffet tables, etc., and launder, dry, fold, hang, and store shirts, towels, skirting, or other dining service items as assigned. Requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, have dexterity and strength in hands and exert up to 35 pounds of force unassisted. Task requires the ability to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions. 10. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1.Successful completion of Cashier Training Class and passing score on final test is required for positions with cashiering duties. 2.Must have clean body, teeth, hair, nails, and clothing. 3.No allergies to soaps, cleaning agents, oven cleaners, or other materials or environmental factors in food service, e.g., steam, dust, etc. 4.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, and University policies, procedures, and communications. 5.Must be able to communicate effectively both orally and in writing in the English language. 6.Must be able to perform all physical and mental requirements outlined in each job duty/responsibility. 7.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: 1.Previous experience in cashiering and using a computerized cash register. Experience in fast food, snack bar, dairy bar, or similar commercial establishment. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact:   University Dining at 765-285-1967. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
