    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Electrician-High-Voltage_R-03440-1": {
      "title": "Electrician/High Voltage",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Electrician/High Voltage Compensation: $42.44 - $42.44 Department: Assoc VP Facilities Planning & Mgt_E (Kevin Ward Start Date: 10/15/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. HOURS 7:00 am to 3:30 pm Monday thru Friday 1st Shift What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform duties related to work in electrical/high voltage maintenance, which involves work in excess of 600 volts, complying with appropriate regulations and codes.   Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Troubleshoot, maintain, and repair the university’s 600-volt, 5 kV and 15 kV distribution systems as required; including electrical manhole sump pumps, transformer vaults, switchgear, fuses, substation equipment, circuit breakers, SF6 vault switches, pad mounted transformers and other components of the campus High Voltage Distribution System. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; use hand tools, power tools, test equipment, power lifts, ladders, scaffolds, etc.; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth, and read small print.     2. Switch loads at vault switches, operate load break elbows at transformers, switch internal building loads, and maintain power and control apparatus. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; use hand tools, power tools, test equipment, power lifts, ladders, scaffolds, etc.; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth, and read small print.     3.   Comprehend, maintain, and utilize campus distribution maps, one-line diagrams, power riser diagrams, control diagrams, equipment specifications and instructions while performing related job functions. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth, and read small print. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral communications and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.     4. Troubleshoot, clean, maintain, repair, and operate the university emergency lighting and power systems as required; including generators, automatic and manual transfer switches, UPS equipment, central inverters, batteries, unit battery exit, emergency lights and distribution and branch circuit panelboards. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; use hand tools, power tools, test equipment, power lifts, ladders, scaffolds, etc.; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth , and read small print. . Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral communications and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   5. Measure, cut, bend, thread, assemble, and install electrical conduits and raceways for systems from one half inch up to 6 inch in diameter. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; use hand tools, power tools, test equipment, power lifts, ladders, scaffolds, etc.; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth , and read small print. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral communications and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   6. Install switches, wiring devices, controls, transformers, distribution apparatus, and install and terminate wires and cables for conductors from size 18  AWG up to 500 KCM rated 300 to 15,000 volts. Phase check, balance, and terminate circuits as required. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; use hand tools, power tools, test equipment, power lifts, ladders, scaffolds, etc.; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth , and read small print.    7. Perform appropriate electrical tests and measurements and analysis of equipment and systems, and report results for evaluation by engineers; including, fluke meters, VLF high potential test, resistive load bank tests automated metering equipment, manual recording of parameters, infrared imaging equipment, and using a personal computer for spread sheets, word processing, ETAP data base, e-mail, and internet research. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; the ability to use hand tools, power tools, test equipment, power lifts, ladders, scaffolds, etc.; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth , and read small print. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral communications and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   8. Provide electrical power for temporary events and scheduled/unscheduled power interruptions as required. This may involve overtime and/or weekend work. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; use hand tools, power tools, test equipment, power lifts, ladders, scaffolds, etc.; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth , and read small print. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral communications and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.     9. Clean, maintain, inventory and manage all department tools and equipment; report all missing components to the supervisor. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; lift up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds constantly; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth , and read small print. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral communications and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   10 . Acquire and maintain knowledge of various job chemicals, environmental concerns, applicable codes and new technologies. Requires the ability to walk, stand, crouch, bend, climb, reach and grasp; exposure to inside/outside environments, extreme temperatures, noise, dirt, and oil; be capable of safely seeing and have normal hearing in areas which range from dim light to bright light and audible sounds and frequency/pressure levels ranging from very low to very high; ability to distinguish color and space depth, and read small print. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral communications and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   11. Perform other related duties as assigned which may arise from time to time. May require any or all of the above-mentioned abilities.   Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent (GED). 1.Successful completion of an apprenticeship program in Electricity as approved by the Bureau of Apprenticeship and Training and two years of post-apprenticeship electrical experience and one year verified proof of experience operating and maintaining energized electrical systems of 4,160 volts or higher, or five (5) years of electrical experience and one (1) of year of operating and maintaining energized electrical systems of 4,160 volts or higher, or equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 2.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, and University policies, procedures and communications, have basic oral/written communication skills, and perform basic mathematical calculations at the level equivalent to first year high school algebra. 3.Must possess basic computer and spread sheet skills. 4.Must possess and maintain a valid Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 5.Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 6.Must be able to respond and be on campus within a reasonable time as determined by Ball State University in an emergency situation. 7.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: Associate's degree in electrical technology. 1. More than one year experience with operating and maintaining energized electrical systems of 4,160 volts or higher. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Kevin Ward, Manager of Building Operations at 765-285-5090 or ksward@bsu.edu Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Must provide all minimum qualifications through attachments and/or completing application to be considered. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Custodian_R-03423-1": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Custodian Compensation: $18.68 - $19.30 Department: Student Center Start Date: 10/25/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. 3rd Shift: 10:30 p.m. to 7:00 a.m. Sunday through Thursday What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform custodial work required for the cleaning and maintenance of facilities complying with appropriate procedures and techniques for equipment and cleaning products. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Clean, renovate, and renew, resilient, wood, and hard floor surface finishes, i.e., dust mop, sweep, wet mop, spot mop, scrub, polish and spray buff, strip, seal, wax, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, balance, stand, walk, push, pull, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of floor machines, wet/dry vacuum, scrubbers, mops, buckets, measuring cups, putty knife, cloth or sponge, eye protection, filter mask, and various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside environmental conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information. 2. Maintain carpet floor coverings, i.e., vacuum, remove spots and stains, extraction cleaning of carpet and upholstered furniture, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, stand, walk, push, pull, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of carpet vacuum, shampooer, wet/dry vacuum, extractor, putty knife, sponge or cloth, eye protection, and various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside environmental conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   3. Clean and service all areas in restrooms to include, but not limited to, lavatory, toilet, urinal, showers, bathtub areas, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, balance, stand, climb, walk, push, pull, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of floor machine, wet/dry vacuum, portable vacuum, hand duster, bucket and wringer, mops, brushes, ladder, sponge, eye protection, gloves, and various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside environmental conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions, information.   4. Dust, vacuum, clean and/or polish furniture and surfaces; clean facilities, fixtures, hardware and windows; change lighting and clean fixtures as required. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, balance, stand, climb, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of dust mop, portable vacuum, hand duster, counter brush, ladder, scaffolds, screwdriver, spray bottle, bucket, sponge, cloth, eye protection, filter mask, light bulbs and tubes, various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside working conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   5. Collect and dispose of trash, refuse, recycling materials and debris into designated receptacles. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, balance, walk, push, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, etc. Task requires the use of trash carts, bags and cans, dollies, gloves, etc. Task exposes employees to inside and outside environmental conditions, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   6. Sweep debris, and/or sweep or shovel snow from outside entrances, landings, steps, walks, etc.; clean exterior surfaces of windows, doors, and other building fixtures. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, stand, walk, lift, push, pull, grasp, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of brooms, snow shovel, plastic bags, squeegee, pole, rags, towels, etc. Task exposes employees to inside and outside working conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   7. Acquire and maintain knowledge of job-related chemicals, and environmental, health and physical concerns. Requires the physical ability to exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend and follow written instructions, procedures, precautions, etc., used in connection with custodial related work, trade publications, department handbook, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   8. Lock and unlock doors as required to perform job related duties in accordance with departmental policies and procedures. Requires the physical ability to stoop, reach, stand, walk, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distance, shape, shadows, etc. Task requires the use of keys. Task exposes employees to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   9 . Set up audio visual equipment in meeting rooms and lounges: Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, climb, stand, walk, lift, push, pull, grasp, and exert in excess of 50 pounds of force occasionally, 20 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, etc. Task requires the ability to operate VCR’s, monitors, cassette players, record players microphones, sound systems, VIS system and various other audio-visual equipment. Task exposes employees to inside and outside environmental conditions, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend and follow written directions and materials. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information the mental ability to use good judgement and discretion.   10. Guide, assist and instruct student custodial employees. Requires the ability to use machines, tools and equipment, as well as the ability to achieve results through student employees, give clear directions, monitor performance and give feedback. Task requires the ability to communicate effectively with people on a one-on-one basis which includes clarity, organization of thought and expressiveness, writing any necessary documentation, be detail-oriented and perform basic mathematical calculations.   11. Set rooms according to custodial worksheet and customer specification; arrange, move and/or replace furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment from room to room as required; report all items requiring repair to supervisor and/or group leaders; perform minor repairs to furniture and building fixtures. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, climb, stand, walk, lift, push, pull, grasp, and exert in excess of 50 pounds of force occasionally, 20 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, etc. Task requires the mental ability to effectively communicate with people on a one-on-one basis which includes clarity organization of thought. Task requires the ability to use good judgement discretion, independence, and to read and comprehend computerized custodial worksheets.   12. Perform other duties as assigned.   Minimum Qualifications: 1.     High School diploma or equivalent (GED). 2.     No allergies to soaps, cleaning agents, chemicals or environmental factors in custodial service. 3.     Must be able to climb ladders, scaffolding of various heights to perform duties. 4.     Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures and communications, and perform basic mathematical functions. 5.     Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 6.     Must successfully pass manlift certification, if position requires it, within a reasonable period of time after hire. 7.     Must have at least one year’s work experience (full time or part time). 8.     You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in custodial work. Knowledge of audiovisual equipment.   How to apply: For additional information please contact James Conner at jmconner@bsu.edu or 765-285-1926 Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Open-Education-Librarian_R-03463": {
      "title": "Open Education Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Open Education Librarian Compensation: $50,000 - $52,000 Department: University Libraries_C About this opportunity: The Ball State University Libraries seeks an Open Education Specialist to lead the University Libraries’ programs and services supporting the creation, adaptation, and adoption of open educational resources (OER), tools, and practices. Working with University Libraries’ colleagues, campus partners, faculty, and students, the successful candidate will prioritize the development of a robust, high impact open textbook grant program and provide leadership and expertise in the areas of scholarly communication, author’s rights, open access, and OER. We seek a curious and creative individual to join our growing team! We welcome early candidates who are seeking to launch a career in open education/textbook publishing and/or mid-career candidates seeking professional growth. The successful candidate can be hired as a specialist or librarian depending on the degree. Applicants are encouraged to think broadly about and communicate how their skills and experiences transfer to the position qualifications, including in ways that may not be obvious, such as how non-library-specific skills and experiences speak to the position responsibilities.  What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function Lead the University Libraries’ programs and services supporting the creation, adaptation, and adoption of open educational resources (OER), tools, and practices; develop a robust, high impact open textbook grant program; provide leadership and expertise in the areas of scholarly communication, author’s rights, open access, and OER; support a collaborative work environment and service culture in order to advance the strategic direction of the University Libraries. Job Duties: In coordination with the Senior Director, develop and lead the University Libraries’ open textbook initiatives through user-focused research and engagement with students, faculty, staff, and campus stakeholders; participate in a network of campus partners to help establish policies, priorities, and outreach for open access publishing and open textbook initiatives. Plan, deliver, and assess open textbook initiatives, including initiatives to encourage and support the use and development of OERs, events, publications, workshops, training opportunities, and internal outreach for library and campus colleagues. Provide education, support and guidance on the discovery, adoption, adaption, creation, and publishing of open and accessible textbooks; promote and serve as a point of contact for general scholarly communication topics such as Creative Commons licensing, author’s rights, publishing models, and open access. Collaborate with library colleagues and campus partners to assess, implement, and maintain platforms, metrics, and resources that support the creation and use of OER; identify and support the needs of OER authors/adapters. Participate in program and unit assessment; track and assess the impact of OER initiatives and activities; interpret, analyze, and evaluate procedures, processes, and program needs; make recommendations for improvements and/or changes to Senior Director. Align planning, priorities, goals, and services with the strategic initiatives of the University Libraries and the University; collaborate with campus partners and student organizations to align the open education initiatives with campus, state, and national directions in open education. Actively participate in and positively contribute to the activities of the University Libraries, university, and profession through such opportunities as related professional organizations, presentations, committee service, publication, etc.; keep abreast of professional literature and scholarly developments in areas of specialization and pursue opportunities for relevant professional development. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: MLS/MLIS/MIS degree from an ALA accredited program such as education or instructional design. Other relevant degrees will also be considered.   Experience identifying, assessing, and/or using open educational resources; experience with teaching and/or library public service; academic library experience Effective oral and written communication skills; ability to collaborate with colleagues in an academic setting Preferred Qualifications: Experience with copyright, fair use, author’s rights, publishing lifecycles, or AI-assisted tools Experience with OER creation and/or adoption, including software and workflows for organizing and providing access to OER Experience with project management, teaching, training, publishing, or editing Knowledge of accessibility best practices Experience with graphic design Additional advanced degrees How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Libraries, Dean's Office at 765-285-5277.   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below:    NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Resume   Cover Letter   Master's Transcripts (optional)  Applications must be received by November 22, 2026, at 12:01 AM.  What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/PT-Food-Service-Cashier_R-01674": {
      "title": "PT Food Service Cashier",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: PT Food Service Cashier Compensation: $16.44 - $16.44 Department: North Dining_F Start Date: 03/15/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Dining has an opportunity for a PT Cashier position. Come and join the Ball State University Dining team on the beautiful Ball State campus and help create excellent customer service experiences for students, faculty, staff and employees! This position may work up to 32.5 hours per week. Hours: (Two week) Sunday: Off Monday: 4p-10p Tuesday: 4p-10p Wednesday: 1:30p-10p Thursday: 4p-10p Friday: Off Saturday: 2p-10:30p Sunday: 2p-10:30p Monday: 4p-10p Tuesday: 1:30p-10p Wednesday: 4p-10p Thursday: 4p-10p Friday: Off Saturday: Off Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform duties related to collection and recording of monies. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Count, wrap, and verify money. Keep money and reports secure at all times. Requires the ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, efficiently operate a calculator, read and comprehend written materials, and be detail-oriented. 2. Open on time and maintain published meal service hours. Requires the ability to walk/stand for extended periods of time. Task requires the visual ability to direct customers to key areas. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. 3. Operate electronic terminals with a high degree of accuracy in logging on, completing cash transactions, completing cash equivalency and debit account transactions, and generating a detailed daily media report at the end of each meal. A high degree of accuracy is expected. Requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, have dexterity and strength in hands, and exert up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and 10 pounds of force frequently. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth. 4. Prepare a manual ‘Check Out Form’ to report all monies from sales and to account for sales ‘overage’ and ‘shortage’. Form must be neatly written and completely accurate. Frequent overage or shortage is not acceptable. Requires the ability to read and comprehend written materials, perform basic mathematical calculations, grasp and handle objects, and be detail-oriented. Task requires the ability to provide written instructions and information. 5. Customer transactions must be made speedily; interact with customers with a smile, courtesy, friendliness, and helpfulness, and communicate customer concerns, questions, comments, and compliments to supervisor. Requires the ability to use computerized card reader, cash register, terminals, calculators, and scales. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions. 6. Maintain cash terminal, scales (where applicable), and other equipment in good condition through correct operation and cleaning procedures. Report equipment malfunctions immediately. Requires the ability to read and comprehend written materials and efficiently operate computerized machinery. Task requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, and have dexterity and strength in hands. 7. Maintain cleanliness, neatness, attractive product display, and good organization of all areas around and including cashier station. May require any of the above-mentioned abilities . 8. Enforce all rules and regulations, including but not limited to: observation of the servery, dining room and grocery areas for possible theft such as pocketing food items or not paying; In all-you-care-to-eat locations, admit only those who have a valid meal plan or who have paid; Permit carry-out according to policy and procedures; Report all violations immediately to management. May require any of the above-mentioned abilities. 9. May be required to: wash and clean dining room conveyors, tables, chairs, service areas, other furnishings, window sills, plants, and equipment located in dining room, serve or re-supply food, snack foods, and other items, instruct dining room attendants in performance of work, assist with special meals or events, i.e., napkin folding, draping and skirting tables, placing decorations, dishing foods, setting up buffet tables, etc., and launder, dry, fold, hang, and store shirts, towels, skirting, or other dining service items as assigned. Requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, have dexterity and strength in hands and exert up to 35 pounds of force unassisted. Task requires the ability to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions. 10. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1.Successful completion of Cashier Training Class and passing score on final test is required for positions with cashiering duties. 2.Must have clean body, teeth, hair, nails, and clothing. 3.No allergies to soaps, cleaning agents, oven cleaners, or other materials or environmental factors in food service, e.g., steam, dust, etc. 4.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, and University policies, procedures, and communications. 5.Must be able to communicate effectively both orally and in writing in the English language. 6.Must be able to perform all physical and mental requirements outlined in each job duty/responsibility. 7.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: 1.Previous experience in cashiering and using a computerized cash register. Experience in fast food, snack bar, dairy bar, or similar commercial establishment. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Dining at 765-285-1967. Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents.    Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration) 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/PT-Food-Service-Worker_R-03028": {
      "title": "PT Food Service Worker",
