    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Custodian-Relief-and-Project_R-03043-1": {
      "title": "Custodian Relief and Project",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Custodian Relief and Project Compensation: $18.68 - $19.30 Department: Noyer Halls Start Date: 11/02/2026 About this opportunity: Saturday-Wednesday 7:30-4:00 PM, off Thursday and Friday. This position is to fill in for the south neighborhood buildings and any open area at Park Hall.  A valid driving license is required for this position. Ball State University Housing has an opportunity for a Custodian Relief and Project. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefit package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! This is a full-time, on-campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform custodial work required for the cleaning and maintenance of facilities complying with appropriate procedures and techniques for equipment and cleaning products. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Clean, renovate, and renew resilient, wood, and hard floor surface finishes, i.e., dust mop, sweep, wet mop, spot mop, scrub, polish and spray buff, strip, seal, wax, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, balance, stand, walk, push, pull, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of floor machines, wet/dry vacuum, scrubbers, mops, buckets, measuring cups, putty knife, cloth or sponge, eye protection, filter mask, and various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside environmental conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information. 2. Maintain carpet floor coverings, i.e., vacuum, remove spots and stains, extraction cleaning of carpet and upholstered furniture, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, stand, walk, push, pull, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of carpet vacuum, shampooer, wet/dry vacuum, extractor, putty knife, sponge or cloth, eye protection, and various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside environmental conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   3. Clean and service all areas in restrooms to include, but not limited to, lavatory, toilet, urinal, showers, bathtub areas, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, balance, stand, climb, walk, push, pull, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of floor machine, wet/dry vacuum, portable vacuum, hand duster, bucket and wringer, mops, brushes, ladder, sponge, eye protection, gloves, and various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside environmental conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions, information.   4. Dust, vacuum, clean and/or polish furniture and surfaces; clean facilities, fixtures, hardware and windows; change lighting and clean fixtures as required. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, balance, stand, climb, walk, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of dust mop, portable vacuum, hand duster, counter brush, ladder, scaffolds, screwdriver, spray bottle, bucket, sponge, cloth, eye protection, filter mask, light bulbs and tubes, various chemical products, etc. Task exposes employees to inside working conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   5. Collect and dispose of trash, refuse, recycling materials and debris into designated receptacles. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, balance, walk, push, pull, lift, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, etc. Task requires the use of trash carts, bags and cans, dollies, gloves, etc. Task exposes employees to inside and outside environmental conditions, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   6. Sweep debris, and/or sweep or shovel snow from outside entrances, landings, steps, walks, etc.; clean exterior surfaces of windows, doors, and other building fixtures. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, stand, walk, lift, push, pull, grasp, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of brooms, snow shovel, plastic bags, squeegee, pole, rags, towels, etc. Task exposes employees to inside and outside working conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   7. Clean appliances, i.e., stoves, ovens, microwaves, refrigerators, ice machines, washers, dryers, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, push, pull, lift, grasp, balance, climb, stand, walk, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distances, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the use of buckets, spray bottles, ladder, sponge, cloth, scrubbing pad, chemicals, etc. Task exposes employees to inside environmental conditions, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   8. Acquire and maintain knowledge of job-related chemicals, and environmental, health and physical concerns. Requires the physical ability to exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend and follow written instructions, procedures, precautions, etc., used in connection with custodial related work, trade publications, department handbook, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   9. Lock and unlock doors as required to perform job related duties in accordance with departmental policies and procedures. Requires the physical ability to stoop, reach, stand, walk, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, inspect areas, judge distance, shape, shadows, etc. Task requires the use of keys. Task exposes employees to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   10. Change bed linens, make beds with clean linens as required. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, lift, reach, stand, walk, push, pull, grasp, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to inspect areas, judge distances, size, shape, shadows, etc. Task requires the use of linens, carts, etc. Task exposes employee to inside environmental conditions, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   11. Arrange, move, and/or replace furniture, supplies, and equipment as required; report items requiring repair to supervisor; perform minor repairs to furniture and building fixtures. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, climb, stand, walk, lift, push, pull, grasp, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to inspect areas, judge distances, shape, shadow, etc. Task requires the use of screwdrivers, pliers, ladder, cart, etc. Task exposes employees to inside and outside environmental conditions, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   12. Load and unload trucks and/or other vehicles, place and store deliveries, etc., inform supervisor of needed supplies. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, push, pull, grasp, climb, balance, stand, walk, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Task requires the visual ability to inspect areas, judge distance, shape, shadows, etc. Task requires the use of cutting devices, ladders, carts, etc. Task exposes employees to inside and outside environmental conditions, fumes, odors, dust, gases, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information.   13. Guide, assist and instruct student custodial employees. Requires all the above listed mental and physical abilities.   14. Set rooms according to custodial work sheet and customer specifications; arrange, move, and/or replace furniture, supplies, and miscellaneous equipment from room to room as required; report items requiring repair to supervisor and/or group leaders; perform minor repairs to furniture and building fixtures, if position requires it. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, climb, stand, walk, lift, push, pull, finger, grasp, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to judge distances and interpret size, shape, and shadow. Task requires the use of screwdrivers, pliers, hammer, ladder, cart, etc. Employees are exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, heights, etc. Task requires mental ability to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions, and receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions.   15 . Mobilize fully loaded trash dumpster; push/pull dumpster to loading dock, push/pull dumpster to compactor, secure dumpster to compactor, mobilize empty dumpster, if position requires it. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, balance, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, stand, walk, and exert up to 68 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read written materials, judge distances, shape, shadows, distinguish colors, etc. Task requires the mental ability to receive and follow oral instructions and to read, comprehend and follow written instructions and information. Task exposes employees to inside/outside environmental conditions, noise, chemicals, fumes, odors, dust, gases, vibrations, heat, oils, etc.   16. Perform other duties as assigned.   Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School diploma or equivalent (GED) 2. No allergies to soaps, cleaning agents, chemicals or environmental factors in custodial service. 3. Must be able to climb ladders and scaffolding of various heights to perform duties. 4. Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures and communications, and perform basic mathematical functions. 5. Must possess and maintain a valid Drivers License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy, if required by assignment. 6. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 7. Must successfully pass manlift certification, if position requires it, within a reasonable period of time after hire. 8. Must have at least one year work experience (full time or part time). 9. You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Experience in custodial work.   How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Natasha Wilson nnwilson@bsu.edu. A valid driving license is required for this position.  Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents.  Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Food-Service-Custodian_R-03527": {
      "title": "Food Service Custodian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Food Service Custodian Compensation: $18.68 - $19.30 Department: Student Ctr Tally Food Court_D Start Date: 10/28/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Dining has an opportunity for a Food Service Custodian position. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefit package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! The ideal candidate will possess great customer service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on-campus opportunity. Hours: (Two Week) Sunday: 8:45a-5:15p Monday: Off Tuesday: 12:30p-9p Wednesday: 12:30p-9p Thursday: 12:30p-9p Friday: 12:30p-9p Saturday: Off Sunday: Off Monday: 12:30p-9p Tuesday: 12:30p-9p Wednesday: 12:30p-9p Thursday: Off Friday: 12:30p-9p Saturday: 8:45a-5:15p Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform routine heavy labor duties in a food service area. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Organize, scrape, prewash, lift and rack items to be washed, set up and operate pan washing machine, store items, maintain sanitary work area. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, finger, reach, grasp, walk and/or stand for extended periods of time, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read cleaning compound labels, directions, visually inspect pots and pans for cleanliness, etc. Task requires the ability to use mechanical pan machine, scrapers, pans soak dish rack, cleaning compounds, water spray nozzle, and garbage disposal. Task exposes employee to various working conditions such as steam heat, noise, chemical cleaning supplies, etc. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   2. Sweep, mop and scrub floors, wash walls, and ceilings throughout food service areas. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, reach, grasp, stretch, push, pull, climb, walk, stand, lift, balance, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read item labels and directions, perceive depth, etc. Task requires the ability to use mops, buckets with manual wringers, brooms, ladders, electric buffers, electric floor scrubber, manual scrapers, etc. Task exposes employee to various working conditions such as vibration, chemical cleaning supplies, atmospheric conditions, etc. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow and provide written instructions and information. 3. Clean greasy or soiled food service areas and equipment including but not limited to tops of refrigerators and ovens, motors, air filters, dirt system, vents, walls and ceilings, etc. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, reach, grasp, push, pull, climb, walk, stand, lift, balance, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, up to 25 pounds of force frequently, and up to 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, read labels, etc. Task requires the ability to use mechanical pan machine, ladders, mops and buckets, manual wringers, cleaning compounds, goggles, masks, gloves, etc. Task exposes employee to various working conditions such as steam heat, vibration, chemicals, atmospheric changes, etc. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   4. Clean, renovate, and renew floor surfaces and finishes including carpet maintenance; perform other cleaning duties including, but not limited to, cleaning food service equipment, windows, ceiling fixtures, etc.; change light bulbs/tubes; clean and resupply restrooms. Requires the physical ability to stoop, bend, crouch, reach, stretch, push, pull, climb, balance, walk, stand, kneel, grasp, reach and clean overhead for extended periods of time, etc. Task requires the visual ability to read label directions, perceive depth, etc. Task requires the ability to use electrical buffers, dust mops, brooms, ladders, goggles, masks, gloves, chemical cleaning supplies, mops and buckets, manual wringers, brushes, etc. Task exposes employee to various working conditions such as a close area for a few hours during work shift, vibration, chemical cleaning supplies, atmospheric changes, etc. Task requires the ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   5. Dispose of trash, refuse and waste materials; clean refuse containers and areas. Requires the physical ability to bend, stoop, reach, grasp, walk, stand, push, pull several times during a work shift, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, up to 25 pounds of force frequently, and up to 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read labels and directions, perceive depth, etc. Task requires the ability to use garden hose and nozzle, trash containers, mechanical industrial trash compactor, gloves, etc. Employee complies with University Waste Management procedures. Task exposes employee to outside environmental conditions and chemicals. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, and understand and apply universal precautions.   6. Lock and unlock food service areas to ensure security. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, stand, walk, push, pull, grasp, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, up to 25 pounds of force frequently, and up to 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth. Task requires the ability to grasp, handle, and use keys, allen wrench, etc. Task exposes employee to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to be attentive to detail and precise .   7. Obtain and deliver supplies and materials as necessary. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, push, pull and grasp items, lift arms overhead and stack stock 6’ high, operate flat bed skid, dolly, various carts several times during work shift, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the ability to write food amounts and the visual ability to read labels, directions and warnings, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task exposes employee to inside and outside environmental conditions, including freezer conditions. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, lists, and labels.   8. Train and direct student personnel as assigned. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, stand, walk, push, pull, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, up to 25 pounds of force frequently, and up to 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the ability to use mops and buckets, manual wringers, brooms, trash containers, trash compactor when giving instructions, etc. Task exposes employee to mostly inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 9. Maintain correct safety and sanitation standards. Requires the visual ability to distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task requires the ability to read, comprehend labels, directions, procedures and policies, universal precautions, etc. Task exposes employee to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to analyze situations, use good judgement, be precise, follow procedures set by management, etc. Task requires the ability to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 10. Lift heavy objects as needed. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, stand, walk, push, pull, grasp several times during work shift, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read a scale, read label directions and perceive depth. Task requires employee to use an analog and/or digital scales, flat bed carts with dollies and 2-wheel carts, etc.   11. Receive, store, inventory and issue food supplies and equipment as assigned, involves lifting heavy objects and reading, counting and recording data. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, push, pull, grasp, walk, stand, lift arms overhead to stack stock 6’ high, operate flat bed skid, dolly, 2-wheel cart, 2-wheel barrel cart, mechanical industrial trash compactor, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read food lists, analog and/or digital scales, labels, purchase orders, delivery forms, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task requires employee to be exposed to extreme cold (32 degrees or below), extreme heat (100 degrees or above), atmospheric conditions, chemical cleaning supplies, etc. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, i.e., item lists, labels, food amounts, memos, numbers, perform basic mathematical calculations, scales and use basic calculators. Task requires the ability to analyze problems, use appropriate judgement, adapt to short notice change with multiple tasks and frequent time/space constraints.   12 . Remove, arrange, replace and/or move dining furniture and food service equipment as necessary. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, stand, walk, push, pull, grasp several times during work shift, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires employee to work with dining tables, chairs, various pieces of kitchen, cooking, and/or storage carts, etc. Task exposes employee to inside environmental conditions. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, room arrangement diagrams and labels.   13 . Assist with dishwashing and storage. Requires the physical ability to kneel, reach, stoop, crouch, stand, walk, push, pull, grasp during work shift, etc. Task requires employee to use mechanical dishmachine, dish and glass dispensers, cleaning compounds, goggles, mask, gloves, racks, spray nozzles, garbage disposal, conveyor, etc. Task exposes employee to inside environmental conditions, mechanical parts, heat, chemical cleaning supplies, noise, etc. Task requires ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   14 . Date and price stock items as needed. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, stand, walk, finger, grasp during work shift, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, up to 25 pounds of force frequently, and up to 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires employee to work with flat bed skid with dolly, 2-wheel cart, marking pens, 2-wheel barrel cart, mechanical industrial trash compactor, etc. Task requires the visual ability to read pricing sheets, numbers, dates of different type size, distinguish color, and perceive depth. Task exposes employee to inside and outside environmental conditions, atmospheric conditions, etc. Task requires the mental ability to use basic math skills such as counting, reading a scale and use a basic calculator.   15 . Perform other duties as assigned.     Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School diploma or equivalent (GED). 2. Must have clean body, teeth, hair, nails, and clothing. 3. No allergies to soaps, cleaning agents, chemicals, or other materials or environmental factors in food service, e.g. steam, dust, etc. 4. Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, and University policies, procedures, communications, and perform basic mathematical calculations. 5. Must be able to perform all physical and mental requirements outlined in each job duty/responsibility. 6. Must have at least one year work experience (full time or part time). 7. You must be 18 years or older Preferred Qualifications: 1. Six (6) months successful employment in a commercial custodial position performing similar duties to those expected at BSU. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Dining at 765-285-1967. Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents.    Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration) 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Maintenance-Group-Leader-2nd-Shift_R-03519": {
      "title": "Maintenance Group Leader-2nd Shift",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Maintenance Group Leader-2nd Shift Compensation: $34.28 - $34.28 Department: Assoc VP Facilities Planning & Mgt_K (Kevin Ward Start Date: 10/27/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. HOURS 3:30 pm to 12:00 midnight Monday thru Friday 2nd Shift What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function Under supervision, the Maintenance Group Leader will be responsible for leading and overseeing a team of skilled tradesmen from various trades. This role requires effective coordination of maintenance activities, ensuring all appropriate regulations and codes are followed. The Maintenance Group Leader will also focus on developing key skills that will help ensure seamless operations in the absence of the Maintenance Supervisor.   Duties & Responsibilities   1. Assist in the assignment and direction of work; evaluate the work performance of assigned employees. Orient and train staff as needed. Duty Requirement Requires the physical ability to stand, walk, climb, balance, push, pull, lift, stoop, crouch, crawl, reach, talk, hear, finger, grasp, detect odors, exert force in the same or opposite directions at the same time, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires ability to distinguish colors, read small print, see and read above and below eye level, and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to keep records, work requests, draw diagrams, specifications, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, noise, vibration, dirt, oils, etc. Task requires mental ability to analyze, read, and comprehend plans, scales, tapes, gauges, etc., read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions and information.   2. Verify and approve material requisitions of employees being supervised. Duty Requirement Requires the physical ability to write, grasp, finger, talk, hear, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend, follow and provide written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information.   3. Obtain supplies and materials from supply houses and storage; monitor inventory levels and prepare paperwork for material requisitions. Duty Requirement Requires the ability to stand, walk, climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, push, pull, left, finger, grasp, write, talk, hear, detect odors, and exert in excess of 100 pounds occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read small print, see and read above and below eye level, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions and noise. Task requires the mental ability to analyze, read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information.   4. Plan work and maintain necessary records. Inspect work in progress and completed work as directed by supervisor. Duty Requirement Requires the ability to sit, stand, talk, hear, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print. Employee is exposed to inside and outside conditions and noise. Task requires the mental ability to analyze, read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information.   5. Perform duties required of skilled trades in the carpentry, electrical, plumbing, or HVAC trades; construct, remodel, maintain, and repair building and facilities. Duty Requirement Requires the physical ability to stand, walk, climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, detect odors, exert force in the same or opposite directions at the same time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish colors, read small print, see and read above and below eye level, and perceive depth. Task requires the use of hand, power, and table equipment related to carpentry, electrical, plumbing, and HVAC trades, ladders and/or scaffolding, computer hardware and software, filter mask, eye and ear protection, protective clothing, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, noise, vibration, dirt, oils, etc. Task requires the mental ability to analyze, read, and comprehend plans, scales, tapes, gauges, etc., receive, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   6. Acquire and maintain knowledge of various job related chemicals, environmental concerns, building codes, and new techniques as required. Monitor and enforce all safety, shop, and university rules and regulations. Duty Requirement Requires the physical ability to sit, stand, talk, hear, see, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions and noise. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   7. Read and interpret drawings and diagrams to ensure compliance with appropriate codes. Duty Requirement Requires the physical ability to see, talk, hear, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions and noise. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   8. Perform other related duties as assigned. Duty Requirement May require any of the above mentioned capabilities.   Minimum Qualifications 1. High school diploma or equivalent G.E.D. 2. Successful completion of an apprenticeship program in Electricity; Plumbing; Heating Ventilation and Air Conditioning; or Carpentry as approved by Bureau of Apprenticeship and Training and two (2) years of experience in one of the above trades, or six (6) years of experience in the above trade(s), or an equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 3. Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, and university policies, procedures, and communications, and to perform mathematical calculations. 4. Must possess and maintain a valid Drivers License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 5. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 6. You must be 18 years or older.   Preferred Qualifications 1. Supervisory experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Brett Wrin, 2nd shift Maintenance Supervisor at 765-285-5804 or brett.wrin@bsu.edu. Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
