    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Payroll-Specialist_R-03497": {
      "title": "Payroll Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Payroll Specialist Salary Grade: Staff 11 Compensation: $18.45 - 20.34 Department: Payroll_A Start Date: 11/08/2026 About this opportunity: Working for Ball State offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical and prescription coverage, dental insurance, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, a university-funded retirement plan, tuition discounts, and more. This is a full-time, on-campus position. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Manage the production of accurate and timely payroll for all employees while working in a deadline driven environment. Responsible for administering organizational polices as well as all federal, state, local, and tax regulations. Provide payroll communication, conduct timekeeper training, analyze payroll data, monitor salary budgets including federal work study and grant funds, ensure proper accounting for all payroll-related transactions, and audit payroll records to secure system and data integrity. Prioritize customer service, identify process improvement needs, and manage special projects related to payroll operations. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Administer the entire payroll process from timecard to paycheck, serving as a subject matter expert for assigned employee group, while maintaining organizational and regulatory compliance. Maintain continual growth of knowledge related to policies, procedures, and regulations as well as continuous review for changes in current policies or regulations as well as make recommendations for procedural changes. 2. Preserve a complete understanding of our timekeeping system to educate employees and timecard managers as well as assist with questions or timecard issues. Audit employee timesheets throughout the pay cycle to ensure accuracy and compliance. Prepare, verify, and upload timekeeping system file (timesheets) into the payroll system. 3. Prepare the payroll system for payroll processing. Audit system tables for correct payroll dates, accurate direct deposits data entry, and complete earnings and deductions records. Review and acknowledge new employee assignments, proofing new jobs information and pay rates from Human Resources for accuracy. Review and correct deduction interfaces from Parking Services, Benefits, and Retirement. Validate garnishments calculations, calculate gross up payments and taxable benefits like moving expense, auto benefits and club dues. 4. Process timely and accurate payrolls in the payroll system. Apply comprehensive knowledge of policies, procedures, and regulations throughout the payroll process to remove roadblocks and resolve issues. Create and maintain the payroll procedures for assigned pay cycle. Review the payroll register for accuracy on new and changed items (earnings and deductions), check gross and net payroll amount for regularity while notating inconsistencies. Produce, confirm for accuracy, and submit the ACH file each pay period. 5. Create, maintain, and utilize files in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and Outlook), Workday, Sprintax, and Timekeeping System (Workday) for auditing purposes and to support data integrity. Generate summarized and detailed reports for distribution each pay period. Monitor labor spend related to federal work study and grant funds and make recommendations for labor redistributions. Identify areas of concerns and propose resolutions or procedural improvements. 6. Ensure accurate accounting for payroll liability accounts. Complete requisitions for disbursement of funds to vendors and journal vouchers for wired funds to vendors both timely and accurately. Assist the Controller’s Office with resolving issues related to liability account reconciliation items. Proactively determine the root cause of the reconciling item, update procedures accordingly, and train other members of the Payroll team. 7. Serve as a payroll liaison. Respond professionally, courteously, and timely to all inquiries in person or via the telephone and email, consistently committing to a superior level of customer service. With a people-centered approach, strive for a people-focused resolution. Advise employees on pay policies, practices, and procedures; make decisions about options and provide them to the employee when possible. 8. Develop payroll communication as necessary, provide training on payroll system to supervisors as needed, make suggestions/recommendations for handbook edits/updates to director, and review and provide recommendations/edits for content on the payroll web page. 9. Manage special projects related to payroll. Implement procedural changes and updates. 10. Perform other related duties as assigned. 11. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or equivalent. At least three years of related experience. Proficient with Microsoft Excel. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution Additional years of related experience. Experience with Workday Human Resources/Payroll. Experience with Workday Timekeeping. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Megan Bryant, Director of Payroll Operations, at mlbryant@bsu.edu . Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: ·         Resume Optional Document: ·         Cover Letter   detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/PT-Crossing-Guard_R-03471": {
      "title": "PT Crossing Guard",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: PT Crossing Guard Salary Grade: Staff 6 Compensation: $11.65 - 12.58 Department: Burris Laboratory School_B Start Date: 11/08/2026 About this opportunity: Burris Laboratory School was established to provide a stellar K-12 educational environment in which pre-service teachers from Ball State University observe and provide learning opportunities for students with highly effective teachers and school counselors using innovative instructional strategies aligned with Indiana standards. This position will perform crossing guard duties required for the safety of Burris Laboratory school students. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform crossing guard duties required for the safety of Burris Laboratory school students.   Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent. Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures and communications. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Requirements: Prior experience in a school environment Duties/Responsibilities: Supervise the crossing of children and other pedestrians at designated crossing locations near assigned school, using traffic control devices and appropriate hand signals, and/or traffic equipment. Demonstrate safe crossing habits for children and prohibits children from committing unsafe practices with regard to pedestrian safety. Ensure student safety by stopping traffic at appropriate intervals. Monitor traffic flow; report unusual or adverse traffic conditions which would have an effect on pedestrian safety. Formal or informal education or training which ensures the ability to read and write at a level necessary for successful job performance. Perform other related duties as assigned. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. The crossing guard works a split shift, reporting for morning arrival time and returning for dismissal time each day. This position works approximately 3 hours per day. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact Brandi Hankins: bshankins@bsu.edu Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Resume Within the application, please provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references. Application Deadline: November 2, 2026, 12:01 a.m."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Director-of-Athletic-Compliance_R-02947": {
      "title": "Director of Athletic Compliance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director of Athletic Compliance Compensation: $47,000-$50,000 Department: Intercollegiate Athletics Ops_G About this opportunity: Join us on the beautiful campus of Ball State University in Muncie, Indiana, supporting 400+ student-athletes within an NCAA Division 1 FBS athletic department. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Coordinate and maintain a program which protects the integrity of Ball State University through compliance with NCAA, Mid-American Conference, and university regulations by student-athletes, coaches, Ball State University employees, and representatives of Ball State University's athletic interests. Duties & Responsibilities 1. Maintain within Ball State University’s Department of Intercollegiate Athletics a culture of compliance with NCAA, Mid-American Conference, and university regulations through effective provision of continuing rules education for all Ball State Department of Intercollegiate Athletics employees; support the development and provision of a compliance orientation program for all new Ball State Department of Intercollegiate Athletics employees; support the development and provision of continuing rules education for Ball State university student-athletes; support development and provision of rules education for representatives of Ball State University’s athletics interests. 2. Participate in the development and implementation of Intercollegiate Athletics compliance and eligibility policies and procedures to ensure full compliance with all NCAA and MAC regulations, including but not limited to analyzing athletics compliance enforcement issues. 3. Serve as a point of contact in matters dealing with student-athlete athletic financial aid, merit based awards and foundation scholarships, pre-enrollment amateurism and waivers. 4. Develop and deliver educational programs to student-athletes, coaches, athletics administrators, staff and others having relationships with the athletics program about University, conference and NCAA rules and regulations. 5. Support Revenue Distribution, and Academic Performance Program Reporting as needed. 6. Serve as a liaison with University units such as Student-Athlete Support Services, Financial Aid, Housing, Office of the Registrar and Rinker Center for Global Affairs (International Programs), etc. 7. Facilitate matters associated with academic and athletic financial aid, foundation scholarships, book scholarships, equipment loans, etc. 8. Serve as compliance liaison for department wide camps and clinics. 9. Support the training and development of the Assistant Director of Compliance, Graduate Assistant and undergraduate interns.  10. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university. 2. Experience in NCAA Division 1 compliance. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Master's degree from an accredited college or university. 2. Three to five years of experience in NCAA Division I compliance. 3. Excellent written and oral communication skills; excellent interpersonal skills; working knowledge of NCAA programs/applications; working knowledge of software systems such as ARMS, Banner, and Compliance Assistant; excellent organizational skills; ability to make informed decisions in a fast-paced and demanding environment; knowledge and familiarity with current and interim NCAA Division I policies and rules, interpretations and education columns.   How to apply: Please provide three professional references at the time of application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter   detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Classroom-Aide_R-02703": {
      "title": "Temporary Classroom Aide",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Classroom Aide Compensation: 14.00 per hour Department: Burris Laboratory School - Temp A Start Date: 08/10/2026 About this opportunity:   Burris Laboratory Schools welcomes applications for Temporary Classroom aide. This position is part-time, working up to 30 hours per week. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function : Burris Laboratory Schools welcomes applications for Temporary Classroom aide. This position is part-time, working up to 30 hours per week. Job Description : Work with K-12 students on a one-on-one basis in academic and social skills development. Provide small group assistance and instruction. Provide supervision during lunch times. Work collaboratively with administrators, faculty, parents, and students. Perform other related duties as assigned. Maintain regular and predictable attendance Minimum requirements : Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Preferred Education and Experience : Associates degree in related field How to apply:   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. Cover Letter Resume"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Biology_R-03405": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor of Biology Compensation: $48,000 - $62,000 Department: Biology Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Biology at Ball State University invites applications for a full-time Non-Tenure-Track Assistant Teaching Professor in Biology. This position is similar to a Research Faculty Fellow position, designed as a bridge position that combines teaching, postdoctoral research, and limited service. The successful candidate will teach primarily in the microbiology concentration of the department, where they will be expected to teach general microbiology along with other undergraduate or graduate courses in their particular area of expertise. Other teaching assignments may include Introductory Biology courses. The successful candidate will be the instructor of record on multiple classes, gain evaluations and feedback on their teaching, and have access to the Department of Online and Strategic Learning to improve teaching. The candidate will be provided a modest start-up package and lab space and will be expected to engage undergraduate and master's students in novel research. The position includes one course release per semester to devote to their research program. We welcome applications from candidates across the full spectrum of microbial sciences. Areas of interest may include—but are not limited to—virology, environmental & ecological microbiology (e.g., microbial ecology, biogeochemistry, soil/aquatic systems), medical/clinical (e.g., immunology, parasitology, mycology), microbial genetics and genomics, applied/industrial microbiology, or microbiome dynamics. Candidates whose research uses interdisciplinary approaches are strongly encouraged to apply. Research activity could be 1) development of an independent research program, 2) continued collaboration with a PhD advisor or previous colleague, 3) development of collaboration with a Ball State faculty member, or 4) some combination of these modes. The department will guarantee support for 1 teaching assistant for all three years. Candidates will be highly encouraged to apply for external funding at the local level and be encouraged to apply for external funding at the federal level in year 2. This position is ideally suited for recent PhD graduates or junior postdocs who are interested in pursuing careers at Primarily Undergraduate Institutions (PUIs) or R2 universities. The candidate will serve on departmental committees, participate in all departmental activities as other faculty do, and be eligible to participate in Search & Selection to gain insight into faculty hiring processes. They will have the opportunity to train undergrad and master’s students, be a member of thesis committees and chair thesis committees, develop an externally funded research program, gain mentorship from other faculty, and have the potential to publish peer-reviewed scientific articles with undergraduate and graduate student co-authors. This is a 9-month, full-time faculty position. This three-year fixed position is renewed on an annual basis. This position is eligible for benefits. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach microbiology at the undergraduate or graduate level. The candidate will develop a research program that engages undergraduate and master's students in novel, cutting-edge research. Minimum Qualifications : Earned doctorate in Biology or related field from an accredited college or university by date of appointment; Commitment to excellence in teaching as demonstrated by a teaching statement and/or teaching evaluations; competency in current laboratory research concepts and approaches. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated teaching ability in Biology using student-centered learning techniques; Evidence of teaching ability or interest, as demonstrated by student or peer evaluation summaries or other activities that indicate an interest in teaching and mentoring students. Evidence of scholarly activity, as demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact Dr. Robert Denton robert.denton@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below. NOTE: Do not use the Autoﬁll feature for resume: Required: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Optional: Master's Transcripts Doctoral Transcripts Applications must be received by December 27, 2026, at 12:01 AM. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-in-Music--Media-and-Production_R-03414": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Music, Media and Production",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Music, Media and Production Compensation: $54,000 - $62,000 Department: School of Music Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The School of Music invites applications for a tenure-line faculty position in Music Media Production with expertise in advanced audio technology and related areas. Areas of specialization may include digital signal processing, audio electronics, audio programming and software development, machine learning, immersive and spatial audio, acoustics, or related fields. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching, maintain an active program of research and/or creative activity, and mentor student research. The School of Music is committed to maintaining a positive, collaborative, and inclusive work environment where your success is supported. This is a full-time opportunity that comes with a great benefits package. Come be a part of our team! This position requires on-campus presence. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Description: The Assistant Professor of Music Media Production will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching, maintain an active program of research and/or creative activity, and mentor student research. Our dynamic faculty function as collaborative, innovative, and adaptive members of the College of Fine Arts community, both within and beyond the School of Music, dedicated as teachers, productive in creative and/or scholarly work, engaged in public service activities, and contributing to the Ball State and Muncie communities and beyond. Additionally, lifelong learning at Ball State University extends educational engagement beyond the classroom and includes learning for professional development, personal enrichment, or other goals throughout one’s lifetime. Faculty will be expected to participate in the department’s, college’s, and university’s lifelong learning opportunities when available and may be assigned teaching responsibility in this area as part of their overall responsibilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Music Media Production in areas aligned with the candidate’s expertise and program needs. Maintain an active program of research and/or creative activity in music technology, audio engineering, or related fields. Mentor undergraduate and graduate research, creative projects, and capstone work. Advise master’s students and, when appropriate, work with doctoral students and serve on graduate committees. Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, and the continued growth of graduate study in Music Media Production. Pursue interdisciplinary collaboration and appropriate industry engagement. Participate in recruitment, program development, and service to the School of Music, College of Fine Arts, University, and profession.   Minimum Qualifications: Education: Master’s degree in music technology, electrical engineering, audio engineering or a related field Experience: Music technology instruction at the University level Proficiency in AVID Pro Tools including AVID S series of control surfaces Proficiency in analog and digital audio equipment Proficiency in basic analog signal flow   Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in music technology, electrical engineering, audio engineering, acoustics, computer science, or a closely related field. Demonstrated expertise in one or more areas including digital signal processing, audio electronics, audio programming, machine learning, immersive or spatial audio, and acoustics. Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate teaching and the ability to teach and mentor graduate students. Experience with technical environments and tools such as MATLAB, Python, C/C++, JUCE, Cycling ’74 Max, Reaktor, or comparable platforms. Professional experience in audio engineering, recording, production, or related industries. Record of scholarly, creative, or professional activity, including publications, album recordings, conference presentations, software or technology development, grants, professional projects, or participation in organizations such as the Audio Engineering Society. How to apply: Please direct inquiries regarding this vacancy to Dr. Franklin Larey, Director of the School of Music, franklin.larey@bsu.edu The following application materials are required: Cover letter of application Curriculum vita e In addition, applicants are asked to provide the contact information of at least three referees. Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by December 2, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Architecture_R-03511": {
      "title": "Instructor of Architecture",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Architecture Compensation: $4500 - $9000 Department: Architecture - Temp Start Date: 01/04/2027 About this opportunity:   The Department of Architecture at Ball State University seeks applicants for multiple part-time semester instructor positions available for a January 2027 or August 2027 start. Please note that applications will remain active for 1 year. Therefore, if you apply for this position, you may not hear from the department until there is a need to hire an instructor. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: This part-time adjunct instructor will teach either design or studio courses to undergraduate and graduate students in the Department of Architecture. Duties and responsibilities will include providing timely feedback and midterm grades to students. Minimum Qualifications: An accredited Master of Architecture degree, master degree of specialization within the discipline of Architecture, or Bachelor of Architecture degree from an accredited institution, or candidate may qualify based on Tested Experience Criteria. Preferred Qualifications: Professional license in Architecture; Master degree in Architecture or related field from an accredited college or university; evidence of quality of design work; evidence of contributions to the profession through professional practice and service; a record of quality teaching experience; evidence of quality scholarship; experience with contemporary design media. How to apply:   For inquiries, please contact: odotson@bsu.edu   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. 1. Curriculum Vitae 2. Cover Letter-Optional 3. Contact information for 3 references Please bundle your documents together to ensure that you can load all required documents."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/University-Dining-Supervisor_R-02646": {
      "title": "University Dining Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: University Dining Supervisor Compensation: $43,888 Department: The Atrium About this opportunity: Ball State University has a professional leadership opportunity available in University Dining that offers an excellent benefits package, paid time off and the opportunity for work/life balance. The University Dining Supervisor position is responsible for directing, overseeing, and leading all food and beverage operations within Ball State University Dining. This position is a closing supervisor. The successful candidate will lead and direct subordinates resulting in good organization and minimal stress, promote teamwork, and execute excellent customer service that exceeds customer expectations. To learn more about Ball State University Dining, please visit our website at: http://www.bsu.edu/campuslife/dining This position supervises full-time and part-time food service workers, cashiers, custodians, group leaders and student employees. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under the direction of the General Manager, oversee and supervise employees in achieving excellence in customer satisfaction, food quality, service of food, employee efficiency and productivity, financial goals, and compliance with safety and sanitation standards, HACCP standards, Indiana Food Service Code regulations, and rules, policies and procedures of Ball State University: additional functions include but are not limited to food service forecasting and record keeping, physical inventory, subordinate training, food and supply purchasing, communication, executing promotions and advertisements, complying with branded concept license and franchise agreements and standards of operations, executing detailed plans and arrangements, contributing to menu, recipe, and concept development, and participating on a limited basis in preparation and serving of food or cashiering. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Lead and supervise employees in executing correct, timely procedures in meeting license/franchise and department standards in relation to the preparation and service of all menu items, including but not limited to recipe preparation, food presentation, quality control, customer service, and sanitation and safety as defined by BSU manuals, handbooks, HACCP standards, Indiana Food Code, NRA ServSafe, and other industry standards; employ excellence in management techniques to exhibit evidence of teamwork and execution of excellent customer service that exceeds customer expectations in such areas, including but not limited to courtesy, speed of service, sense of urgency, product consistency, demonstrating a passion for excellence, utilizing fun and humor when appropriate, innovation and creativity, and other criteria. 2. Orient, coach, and train employees resulting in well-trained employees who consistently exhibit excellence in job knowledge and performance; ensure employees are well trained before working in any job assignment; provide accurate, balanced (positive and negative) feedback to employees regarding job performance and follow up on corrective measures; complete and maintain file documentation for all orientation, coaching, and training of each employee according to departmental procedures. 3. Count safe and audit safe record; audit cashier reports and submit thorough, accurate, cashier check-out reports to bookkeeper; properly report and account for shortages in safe or deposits of sales; complete documentation, report all unaccounted monies (over $20.00) immediately to the General Manager and/or University Police; check and approve all cashier refunds to customers and audit the no sale transactions of each cashier to prevent cashier theft; maintain accurate and up-to-date meal card system, including but not limited to reporting lost cards, verify account status, and overseeing the recording of off line transactions; administer university and departmental policies as they relate to money handling and reporting; ensure cashiers properly ring sales to record product movement and product value related to each brand upon which royalty payments to brand licensors or franchisors are based. 4. Utilize the Cbord Menu Management computer system to prepare menu item forecasts to (a) determine production of foods for service, and (b) correctly submit service statistics for historical data via computer record; under firm deadlines, scrutinize purchase requisitions and approve amounts of foods and supplies to be ordered based upon forecasted projections of sales and menu items, inventory levels, and other indicators; manage purchasing assignment with the utmost in business ethics and following policies and procedures of Ball State University; maintain appropriate inventory levels of foods and supplies as assigned, with neither being over or under-stocked; complete weekly inventory of foods and/or supplies with a high degree of accuracy. 5. Oversee and maintain adequate staffing following University procedures to schedule replacement employees; complete documentation related to scheduling regular and overtime staff; maintain correct telephone and address lists of all employees to facilitate this task; demonstrate a commitment to affirmative action and equal employment opportunity; communicate with peers and subordinates in a thorough, detailed, timely even-handed manner resulting in effective personal contact and/or the completion of management log entries that communicate necessary information to peers; attend shift meetings, unit and departmental management staff meetings, and relate telephone messages and/or other information accurately and in a timely manner; maintain confidentiality and ethical practices as relates to communications; in stressful situations, remain, calm, in control, and have a positive impact on others; manage disagreements effectively and create an environment where peers, employees, and customers are treated with dignity and respect and where rules, policies, and procedures are consistently administered. 6. Evaluate, investigate, and secure approval of General Manager and the Assistant Director of Personnel, or the Director, then issue warranted counseling or discipline to employees in a timely manner according to university policies and procedures; submit written documentation of all investigations, interviews, meetings, or conversations related to the situation in addition to copies of the properly issued disciplinary forms; accurately administer the union agreement and addenda thereto (including absence and tardiness policies and required record-keeping). 7. Unlock facility for the day’s operations and/or secure the facility for the periods of closure; observe safety and security precautions to prevent personal or employee injury, and theft of university or employee property; maintain personal and unit keys in a safe manner to prevent unauthorized use. 8. Establish, evaluate, and execute personal and unit goals, and contribute to departmental goal setting and achievement; serve in a contributory and effective manner on teams, committees, and task forces; demonstrate a professional appearance; wear clean, well-pressed clothing daily; follow prescribed dress code guidelines as outlined in departmental policies, rules, and regulations. 9. Evaluate employee performance and complete timely formal appraisal forms impartially and in an unbiased manner; submit draft appraisals for the approval of the General Manager; properly conduct the performance review meetings with employees; route completed forms in a timely manner. 10. Contribute to optimizing profitability through effective monitoring and supervision of food waste, portion control, inventory management, key control, theft and security controls, proper charging of sales to customers and employees by cashiers, and employees as they use and care for the facility, equipment, and furnishings; assist in evaluating food, labor, and other controllable costs; implement corrective measures as needed. 11. Collaborate in executing an effective marketing and promotion program for the unit in conjunction with the General Manager, approval from the Assistant Director of Personnel, and Assistant Director of Operations. 12. Provide planning of standard and custom menus, submit recipes for new menu items, and assist with development of sales mix for the unit; assist in planning and executing special events, catered events, and other non-routine food services. 13. Coordinate an effective laundry procedure to ensure proper supply of clean linen; maintain neat, accurate, require records; report maintenance and repair needs of building and equipment in a timely manner. 14. Perform food preparation, service and cashiering duties in emergency situations, and/or for short work periods to meet customer demand. 15. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: -Associates degree from an accredited institution or equivalent combination of education, credentials, certification, and experience. -At least one year of direct or related work experience (exclusive of teaching) in commercial or institutional food service, with demonstrated leadership and dynamic team building skills. -Skills in oral and written communication, strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: -Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. -Five years of direct or related work experience (exclusive of teaching) in commercial or institutional food service, with demonstrated leadership and dynamic team building skills supervisory experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Dining at 765-285-1967. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions:  Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents listed below. Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: 1. Resume Optional Document (Recommended for Best Consideration): 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Project-Manager---Video-Editor_R-03565": {
      "title": "Temporary Project Manager & Video Editor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Project Manager & Video Editor Compensation: $15-$20 per hour Department: WIPB - Temp Start Date: 10/27/2026 About this opportunity:   The Project Manager & Video Editor position plays a vital role on the video team at Ball State Public Media. This position acts as project manager for the Now Entering series. The ideal candidate combines strong project management, videography, editing, and storytelling skills. Acts as the logistical backbone for the media team, coordinating production schedules, managing the complete video asset development lifecycle from concept, filming, and final delivery, while communicating professionally with clients. Must be detail oriented and have an excellent understanding of various file formats and codecs. Candidates must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Skills: Strong project management, time management, multi-tasking skills, be comfortable working with Adobe Premiere Pro or comparable professional editing software, strong visual storytelling taste and attention to pacing and viewer retention.   Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Communication Field from an accredited institution. At least two years of experience in video production project management; non-linear editing; and camera operations.   Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Telecommunications or a related field. Three years of experience in video production project management; experience in non-linear editing, such as Adobe Premiere Pro or Final Cut Pro; camera operations, motion graphics creation; video codes; working on shoots or local television, and managing social media campaigns   Duties: 1. Serve as project manager that is responsible for coordinating the Now Entering, or other projects as needed, community meetings, pre-production schedules, calendars, and filming dates with clients and internal teams. 2. Manage asset libraries and organize raw media files after shoots, familiarity with file management and codecs. 3. Coordinate the recording of footage on location as camera operator. 4. Edit videos from beginning to final delivery with strong visual storytelling taste and attention to pacing and viewer retention using non-linear editing software programs. 5. Plan and maintain the social media campaign calendar for the Now Entering project, or other projects as needed. 6. Develop, maintain, and assist colleagues with technical knowledge in an environment with constantly and rapidly changing technology. 7. Other Duties As Assigned   This position may involve traveling to places in Indiana. How to apply:   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Please apply with: Resume Cover Letter a video demo reel and/or portfolio website. For Questions, please contact August Wilde at August.Wilde@bsu.edu"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Info-Systems---Operations-Management_R-03341": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Info. Systems & Operations Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Info. Systems & Operations Management Compensation: $130,000-$135,000 Department: Info Systems & Operations Mgt (Qiannong Start Date: 08/02/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Information Systems and Operations Management in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 2027. We are a student-oriented, industry-connected, and forward-looking department committed to preparing students for successful careers in logistics and supply chain management. Our program emphasizes experiential learning through a required internship, an immersive capstone project, and opportunities to engage with industry professionals. These experiences connect classroom knowledge with real-world business challenges and help students develop the analytical, problem-solving, leadership, and professional skills needed to succeed in a rapidly evolving global supply chain environment. The successful candidate will join the department at an exciting time as we continue to strengthen our curriculum, expand industry partnerships, and enhance experiential learning opportunities. Through the Kent C. \"Oz\" Nelson Logistics and Supply Chain Management Center for Excellence and our industry advisory board, we seek to build meaningful connections among students, faculty, and industry partners. We welcome candidates who bring fresh perspectives, innovative ideas, and a collaborative spirit to support the continued growth of our program. We are seeking a candidate who is committed to excellent teaching, meaningful scholarship, and service that advances student success and program development. The ideal candidate will demonstrate an interest in integrating emerging technologies and industry developments into teaching, including artificial intelligence, supply chain analytics, supply chain resilience, and other innovations shaping logistics and supply chain management. Candidates with an interest and ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in logistics and supply chain management, particularly in one or more of the following areas, are strongly encouraged to apply: supply chain analytics, inventory and procurement management, process management, strategic and global logistics, supply chain integration, and quality management. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Teach nine semester hours each fall and spring semester in subjects such as but not limited to: operations management, inventory management, supply chain analytics, project management, quality management; assignment may include undergraduate and graduate courses, which may be delivered on-line, synchronously or asynchronously. Additional activities will include scholarly activity and service. Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Logistics and Supply Chain Management or closely related fields from an accredited institution. Candidates with ABD will be considered and must demonstrate satisfactory progress toward completion of the doctoral degree consistent with university policy. Evidence of or, demonstrated potential for, high-quality scholarly research and effective university-level teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Record of scholarly publications in peer-reviewed quality journals; experience in creative teaching methods such as experiential-learning, service-learning, immersive-learning, or other instructional innovations; and on-line teaching; evidence of active involvement in external grant writing; business experience in the field of Information Systems or related areas; ability to teach and conduct research in Business Analytics and Information Systems How to apply: Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Do not use the Autofill resume feature.) References: Within the application, you will be prompted to provide the names and contact information for three (3) professional references. Applications must be before submitted before 12:01 AM on 12/4/2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet. Relocation Program: MakeMyMove   Looking for a place where your career, community, and quality of life can grow together? Muncie and Delaware County offer the advantages of a university community with the accessibility and affordability of a mid-sized city—short commutes, local arts and culture, parks and trails, educational opportunities, healthcare, athletics, and a strong sense of connection. Through the City of Muncie’s MakeMyMove program, eligible new residents may access relocation incentives, university-related benefits, co-working options, and community-building opportunities designed to help them get settled and connected. Current benefits for eligible participants may include: Up to $5,000 cash for relocation Co-working space courtesy of The Innovation Connector Access to the Ball State University Library One-semester Rec Fit pass at Ball State University Discounted Ball State Athletics tickets Help desk for connecting to local resources Opportunity for board participation Six-month YMCA membership Relocation programs on MakeMyMove have specific eligibility requirements, and benefits may vary by program. Applicants should review the current MakeMyMove page to confirm eligibility, available benefits, and program status. Ball State’s support for relocation resources and community partnerships aligns with Destination 2040: Our Flight Path , the University’s strategic plan. The plan calls our University to work with community partners to promote talent attraction and retention, foster economic growth in East Central Indiana, and strengthen the economic and social vitality of the communities we serve. Explore the program and check your eligibility through MakeMyMove ."
